hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6001","5997 - Abu al-Sabbah Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt informed us, Umar ibn Miskin informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: I never prayed behind your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but I heard him say when he finished: O Allah, forgive me my sins and deliberate acts; O Allah, guide me to good deeds and morals, for none guides to their good nor averts their evil but You."
"6002","5998 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad informed us, Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah informed us, from Harb ibn Qays, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, loves that His concessions be taken just as He loves that His firm commands be taken, or: just as He dislikes that His disobedience be committed."
"6003","From the hadith of Salim from Ibn Umar. 5999 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to me - he said: I heard it from his mouth, repeating and producing it - from Salim, from his father who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar walking in front of the bier."
"6004","6000 - And Ahmad ibn Abdah informed us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan."
"6005","6001 - Ahmad ibn Abdah informed us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man of the Ansar admonishing his brother about modesty, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Modesty is part of faith."
"6006","6002 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he began the prayer, raise his hands until they were level with his shoulders, and when he wanted to bow, and after he rose from bowing; and he would not raise them between the two prostrations."
"6007","6003 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us of it, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father."
"6008","6004 - And Muhammad ibn al-Layth informed us of it, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us, Bakr ibn Mudar informed us, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet, with similar wording."
"6009","6005 - al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a white shirt on Umar and said: Is this garment of yours new or washed? He said: Washed. He said: Wear new, live praised, and die a martyr. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it except Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father; none corroborated him in it."
"6010","6006 - al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Khalid ibn al-Walid to Banu Jadhimah, and he called them to Islam but they could not say: We have embraced Islam; instead they kept saying: We have changed religion, we have changed religion. And Khalid set upon them with killing and capture, and handed to each man his captive; then in the morning Khalid ordered that each man among us kill his captive. When we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Khalid's deed was mentioned to him, he raised his hands and said: O Allah, I disavow to You what Khalid has done - three times."
"6011","6007 - al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in the Fajr prayer when he raised his head from the second rak'ah, supplicating against some of the hypocrites, whereupon Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: ""You have nothing to do with the matter, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers."""
"6012","6008 - al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by al-Hijr and said: Do not enter the dwellings of those who wronged themselves unless you are weeping, lest there befall you the like of what befell them. Then he hastened until he crossed the valley."
"6013","6009 - And al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrating, he said: I saw tonight that I was brought a cup, and I drank from it until I could see satisfaction flowing, then I gave my remainder to Umar. They said: How did you interpret that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Knowledge."
"6014","6010 - al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on his mount wherever it faced with him."
"6015","6011 - al-Husayn informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a man asked him, saying: I saw Laylat al-Qadr as if it were the night of the twenty-third. He said: I see your dreams have coincided upon the last ten, so seek it in the ten, in the remaining odd nights, in the odd."
"6016","6012 - And with his chain: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will gain power over them - meaning the Jews - until a stone says: O Muslim, this is a Jew - I think he said - so kill him."
"6017","6013 - And with his chain he said: I saw them when the order was given concerning them - meaning the two Jews - that they be stoned; I saw him shielding her with his hand to protect her from the stones. He said: And this verse was revealed concerning that: ""Indeed We sent down the Torah, in it guidance and light; the prophets who submitted judged by it."" And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of them."
"6018","6014 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir informed us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the sperm-drop is created in the womb, the angel of the wombs says: O Lord, what shall I write? So He decrees His command to him; he says: Male or female? So He decrees His command to him, and he writes; and he decrees what he will meet until he dies, even the stumble he stumbles. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, except Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar."
"6019","6015 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani informed us, Umar ibn Qays informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The declining of the sun is its passing the meridian. And this hadith is only narrated stopped (mawquf) from Ibn Umar; none raised it from al-Zuhri except Umar ibn Qays, and he was weak in hadith."
"6020","6016 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that Ghaylan ibn Salamah accepted Islam with ten wives under him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to choose four of them."
"6021","6017 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti informed us of it, Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah informed us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that Ghaylan ibn Salamah accepted Islam with ten wives under him who were with him in pre-Islamic times and accepted Islam with him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to choose four of them. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, except the people of Basra; and he corrupted it in Yemen, narrating it mursal."
"6022","6018 - Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bad omen is in three: the house, the woman, and the horse."
"6023","6019 - Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill the snake with two stripes and the short-tailed one, for they efface sight and cause miscarriage."
"6024","6020 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sufyan informed us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that a people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we entered this house with abundant wealth and became poor, with many in number and our number lessened, and with good relations and our relations soured. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave it, it is blameworthy. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how shall we leave it? He said: Sell it, or give it away. And this hadith, in my view Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar erred in it; al-Zuhri only narrates it from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, mursal."
"6025","6021 - Bishr ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim al-Kirmani informed us, Yunus ibn Yazid informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that he used to send the weak of his family ahead, and they would stand at al-Mash'ar and depart before the people, or before the imam departed. And Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave concession in that to women."
"6026","6022 - al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, Isa ibn al-Mundhir informed us, Baqiyyah informed us, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches a rak'ah of Friday prayer, let him add another to it. And al-Zubaydi contradicted the memorizers in this narration, for the memorizers narrate this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah."
"6027","6023 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Kathir ibn Hisham informed us, Ja'far ibn Burqan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman together with her paternal aunt or maternal aunt. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, except Ja'far ibn Burqan, nor from Ja'far except Kathir ibn Hisham."
"6028","6024 - Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman informed us, al-Ala ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution; and he said: Perform ablution from what fire has changed. And these two hadiths are only narrated from Ibn Umar stopped (mawquf); al-Ala alone raised them."
"6029","6025 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Tinnisi informed us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father who said: Neither the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor Abu Bakr, nor Umar would wear their rings until Aban came to Umar - meaning they would acquire them but not wear them."
"6030","6026 - al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not leave fire in your houses when you sleep."
"6031","6027 - And Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not leave fire in your houses when you sleep."
"6032","6028 - And al-Husayn ibn Mahdi informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to touch the Yemeni corner and the Stone."
"6033","6029 - And with his chain: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed the Isha one night, so Umar called him: The women and children have slept. He said: None of the people of the earth awaits this prayer but you."
"6034","6030 - And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from praying in the mosques."
"6035","6031 - And with his chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The night prayer is two by two; when you fear dawn, then one by which you make it odd."
"6036","6032 - And with his chain: that he used to send ahead the weak of his family, and they would stand at al-Mash'ar, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave permission to the weak of his family."
"6037","6033 - And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Dajjal and said: I warn you of him, and Nuh warned his people of him; but I shall say to you about him what no prophet said to his people: Allah is not one-eyed."
"6038","6034 - And with his chain he said: I saw the people in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being beaten when a man bought food, against selling it until he conveyed it to his dwelling."
"6039","6035 - And with his chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you make his brother stand from his seat and sit in it."
"6040","6036 - And with his chain: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rak'ahs in his house on Friday when he returned."
"6041","6037 - And with his chain: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to al-Hijr and said: Do not enter the dwellings of those who wronged except weeping, lest there befall you what befell them. Then he hastened until he passed the valley."
"6042","6038 - al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Salim who said: I was with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and asked him about tamattu' with Umrah to Hajj, and he said: It is good, no harm. He said: Your father used to forbid it. So Ibn Umar became angry and said: We follow the command of the Messenger of Allah."
"6043","6039 - al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shaved in his Hajj."
"6044","6040 - And with his chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the fear prayer with one of the two groups while the other group faced the enemy; then they withdrew and stood in the position of their companions facing the enemy, then those came and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed a rak'ah with them, then gave salutation, then these made up a rak'ah and those a rak'ah."
"6045","6041 - I copied from the book of Ahmad ibn al-Faraj, from Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade coming to women at night unannounced. When he looked in the book he said: I saw it with me in two places: once from Salim, from his father, and once from Salim. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri except Ibn Abi Dhi'b, nor from Ibn Abi Dhi'b except Ibn Abi Fudayk; and it is well known from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, in the hadith of Ibn Abi Fudayk."
"6046","6042 - Sulayman ibn Ubaydullah al-Ghaylani narrated to us, Abu Amir informed us, Zam'ah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not stung from the same hole twice."
"6047","6043 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar informed us, Yunus ibn Yazid informed us, from al-Zuhri who said: It reached me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stoned the jamrah, stoned it with seven pebbles, saying takbir with each pebble, then descended to its right and stood facing the qiblah raising his hands supplicating, and he would prolong the standing; then he would come to the second jamrah and stone it with seven pebbles, saying takbir each time he threw a pebble, then descend to the left toward the valley and stand facing the House raising his hands supplicating; then he would come to the jamrah at al-Aqabah and stone it with seven pebbles, saying takbir each time he threw a pebble, then leave without standing at it. Al-Zuhri said: I heard Salim narrating this hadith from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And Ibn Umar used to do that. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri except Yunus ibn Yazid."
"6048","6044 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Amir informed us, Ali ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Abu Qilabah narrated to me, Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to me, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A fire is about to emerge before the Day of Resurrection from Hadramawt gathering the people. They said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), what do you command us? He said: Hold to al-Sham. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated in the hadith of Salim, from Ibn Umar, except by the narration of Abu Qilabah."
"6049","6045 - Ahmad ibn Abdah and Hawtharah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, the wording being Ahmad's, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a slave jointly with another and one of them frees his share, if he is wealthy he is assessed the highest value, or assessed a value with neither undervaluation nor excess, then he is freed. And we do not know Amr ibn Dinar al-Makki raised from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) any hadith other than this. Dawud al-Attar narrated it from Amr ibn Dinar, saying: I heard Ibn Umar; and the correct is what Ibn Uyaynah narrated."
"6050","6046 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi informed us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Salim, from his father who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was pressed by travel, he would delay this prayer - meaning Maghrib."
"6051","6047 - And Abdullah ibn Sa'id Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Usamah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab went out to the mosque and found a striped silk cloak, so he returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not buy this cloak to wear when delegations come to you and on Friday? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is only the clothing of one who has no share. Then he remained as long as Allah willed him to remain, then he sent to Umar a brocade cloak that had been gifted to him. Umar came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you sent this to me though I heard you say about it what you said. He said: I did not send it to you to wear; I only sent it for you to sell and use for some of your need, or to clothe some of your women with it."
"6052","6048 - And al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated it to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah informed us, Shu'bah informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"6053","6049 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar informed us of it, Rawh informed us, from Hanzalah, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"6054","6050 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bilal informed us, Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Salim, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Three at whom Allah will not look on the Day of Resurrection: the disobedient to his parents, the addict of wine, and the one who reminds of his giving; and three who will not enter Paradise: the disobedient to his parents, the dayyuth, and the masculine woman."
"6055","6051 - And Amr ibn Ali informed us of it, Abu Asim informed us, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from Abdullah ibn Yasar, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Three at whom Allah will not look on the Day of Resurrection: the disobedient, the dayyuth, and the masculine woman who imitates men; and three who will not enter Paradise: the disobedient to his parents, the one who reminds of his giving, and the addict of wine. And the hadith of Muhammad ibn Amr, we do not know anyone narrated it from him except Imran al-Qattan, nor narrated it from Abdullah ibn Yasar except Umar ibn Muhammad."
"6056","6052 - Isma'il ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Sulayman informed us, Musa ibn Uqbah informed us, from Salim, from his father who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Usamah ibn Zayd, they spoke about him, and that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: What you said about Usamah has reached me, and you said that about his father before him; he is fit for command, and he is the most beloved of people to me. He did not except Fatimah nor anyone else."
"6057","6053 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, Sufyan informed us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from his father who said: The oath of the Messenger of Allah by which the Messenger of Allah would swear was: No, by the Turner of hearts."
"6058","6054 - And Amr ibn Ali informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan informed us, Musa ibn Uqbah informed us, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. So Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, one side of my waist-wrap hangs loose. He said: You are not of those who do it out of pride."
"6059","6055 - Sa'id ibn Yahya narrated to us, as I think my father narrated to me, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw a black woman with disheveled hair go out of Medina until she alighted at Mahya'ah, which is al-Juhfah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) interpreted it that the fever of Medina had moved to al-Juhfah."
"6060","6056 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muslim informed us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes a handspan of land will be collared with it from seven earths."
"6061","6057 - Isma'il ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, Fudayl informed us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he met Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl at the foot of Baldah, before revelation had descended upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered him a travel meal containing meat, and he said: We do not eat what you slaughter upon your stone altars, nor do we eat except what Allah's name has been mentioned over. He said: And Abdullah narrated to me this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6062","6058 - And Ibn Ma'mar informed us of it, from Affan, from Wuhayb, from Musa, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"6063","6059 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Asim informed us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command lightening, though he would lead us with al-Saffat. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ibn Umar except by this route, nor do we know it narrated from anyone other than Ibn Umar either."
"6064","6060 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh informed us, Hanzalah informed us, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw at the Ka'bah a brown man with lank hair placing his hands on two men, his head dripping water; I asked: Who is this? It was said: Isa son of Maryam, or al-Masih son of Maryam. Hanzalah said: I do not know which of the two. He said: And I saw behind him a red man with curly hair, blind in the left eye, the one of those I saw most resembling him being Ibn Qatan, meaning Abd al-Uzza ibn Qatan. I asked: Who is this? They said: al-Masih al-Dajjal."
"6065","6061 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah informed us, from Hanzalah, from Salim, from his father who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), pointing toward Iraq: Tribulation is here; tribulation is from where Satan's two horns rise."
"6066","6062 - And Amr ibn Ali informed us of it, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, Layth, meaning Ibn Abi Sulaym, informed us, from Salim, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Tribulation is here - meaning toward the east."
"6067","6063 - And Uqbah ibn Mukram informed us of it, Abu Asim informed us, Umar ibn Muhammad informed us, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet, with similar wording."
"6068","6064 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, my father narrated to me, he said: I heard Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: I heard my father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Tribulation comes from the east, from where Satan's horn rises; and you will strike one another's necks. And Allah, blessed and exalted, said to Musa: ""And you killed a soul, then We saved you from distress and tried you with trials."""
"6069","6065 - And Ali ibn al-Mundhir informed us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, Layth informed us, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a bier has a qirat, and awaits it until it is buried has two qirats."
"6070","6066 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, Layth informed us, he said: I heard Salim, he said: My father narrated to me that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever makes an image will be charged with giving it life on the Day of Resurrection."
"6071","6067 - And Ubaydullah ibn al-Jahm informed us, Damrah ibn Rabi'ah informed us, Ibn Shawdhab informed us, from Tawbah al-Anbari, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless for us our Sham and our Yemen, our mudd and our sa'."
"6072","6068 - al-Qasim ibn Bishr ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi' al-Sa'igh informed us, Asim ibn Umar informed us, from Bilal ibn Abi Bakr, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Every intoxicant is forbidden, and whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is forbidden."
"6073","6069 - Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Dirhami informed us, Anas ibn Iyad Abu Damrah informed us, Musa ibn Uqbah informed us, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"6074","6070 - And al-Fadl ibn Sahl informed us, Nuh ibn Maymun informed us, Ibrahim ibn Mas'ud informed us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"6075","6071 - And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Consult women concerning themselves."
"6076","6072 - And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj. 6073 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and Muhammad ibn Mirdas informed us, both said: Rawh ibn Ubadah informed us, from Hanzalah, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever keeps a dog that is neither a livestock dog nor a hunting dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day. And he said in the hadith of Bukayr: A hunting dog, or a livestock dog."
"6077","6074 - Amr ibn Ali and Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, both said: Abu Asim informed us, Umar ibn Muhammad informed us, Salim narrated to me, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"6078","6075 - And Abdah ibn Abdullah informed us of it, Muhammad ibn Bishr informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Salim, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: I saw in a sleeper's dream as if I were at a well and people gathered at it; Abu Bakr came and drew a bucket or two, with weakness in his drawing, and Allah forgives him. Then Umar came and it turned into a large bucket in his hand, and I never saw a genius working like his working, until the people watered their camels. And the wording is the wording of Umar ibn Muhammad, and the hadith of Ubaydullah is similar. And we do not know anyone narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah except Muhammad ibn Bishr."
"6079","6076 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Salim, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever lies about me, a house is built for him in the Fire."
"6080","6077 - Ubayd ibn Isma'il al-Habbari narrated to us, Abu Usamah informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar informed us, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the meat of domestic donkeys. And Ubaydullah narrated hadiths from Salim, heard from him, and raised two hadiths from him."
"6081","6078 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi informed us, from Hanzalah, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not strike the face."
"6082","6079 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi informed us, Hanzalah informed us, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When women ask your permission to go to the mosques at night, permit them. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr on his mount."
"6083","6080 - Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Khuthaym al-Hilali informed us, Hanzalah informed us, from Salim, from his father who said: I heard him say: Come, let me bid you farewell as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bid us farewell: I entrust to Allah your religion, your trust, and the outcomes of your deeds."
"6084","6081 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, both said: Abu Asim informed us, Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar informed us, Salim narrated to me, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"6085","6082 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar informed us of it, Abu Asim informed us, Umar ibn Muhammad informed us, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: That one's belly be filled with pus is better for him than that it be filled with poetry. And the hadith of Umar ibn Muhammad, we heard it only from Ibn Ma'mar; this hadith is only known by the narration of Abu Asim, from Abu Ubaydah, from Salim. And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar brought out to us the hadith of Abu Asim, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from the original of his book."
"6086","6083 - Amr ibn Ali and Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, both said: Abu Asim informed us, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from Salim, from his father who said: We used to say in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman - meaning in the caliphate. And this hadith is narrated from Ibn Umar by other routes, that he said: We would not prefer any of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over another, and we would say: Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman, then we would not prefer after that. And Umar ibn Muhammad was not a memorizer, and that is evident in his hadith when he narrates from other than Salim."
"6087","6084 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal informed us, Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, from Salim, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, forbids you to swear by your fathers."
"6088","6085 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Qabisah ibn Uqbah informed us, Sufyan informed us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"6089","6086 - And Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Baghdadi informed us of it, Ishaq ibn Yusuf informed us, Sufyan informed us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man makes an image but it is said to him: Give life to what you created."
"6090","6087 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id and Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu al-Jawwab, from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three garments. And Abu al-Jawwab erred in this hadith from al-Thawri; the memorizers narrated it - Abd al-Rahman and others - from Sufyan, from Asim, from Salim, from his father: that Umar was shrouded in three garments."
"6091","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Farwah ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud al-Jazari narrated to us, saying: I heard Salim and Nafi' narrating from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said concerning tayammum with earth: that you strike the dust with your palms, then wipe your face with them, then strike another blow and wipe your forearms with them up to the elbows. This hadith was narrated by Sulayman from Nafi' and Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but the precise memorizers stop it at the statement of Ibn Umar."
"6092","Although Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Asri also narrated it from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated it to us: Muhammad ibn Thabit narrated to us."
"6093","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us: Qudamah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"6094","Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam also narrated it to us: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. This hadith has been narrated from Ibn Umar through several chains: Salim, Nafi', Abdullah ibn Dinar, Zayd ibn Aslam and others narrated it. We have repeated it only because Qatadah did not narrate anything from Salim, from his father, except this hadith; had we omitted it, the hadith of Qatadah from Salim would have been lost. And Qudamah ibn Musa did not narrate from Salim, from his father, anything except this hadith."
"6095","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Amir narrated to us: Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, saying: I heard Salim ibn Abdullah narrating from his father that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting for a believer to be one who curses frequently. We do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Salim, from his father, except Kathir ibn Zayd, and we do not know that Kathir ibn Zayd narrated from Salim anything except this hadith."
"6096","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us: Uqbah ibn Abi al-Sahba' narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father, who said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among some of his Companions, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you not know that I am the Messenger of Allah to you? They said: We bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you not know that Allah, blessed and exalted, revealed in His Book that whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah? They said: We bear witness that whoever obeys you has obeyed Allah; Allah has commanded obedience to you. He said: {Obey Allah and obey the Messenger} - for obedience to Allah is obedience to me, and obedience to me is that you obey your leaders; if he prays sitting, then pray sitting."
"6097","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Use ithmid (antimony), for it grows the hair and clears the vision."
"6098","Amr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar both narrated to us, saying: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Uthman, from Salim, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Use the black seed, for in it is a cure for every disease except death (al-sam). These two hadiths - we do not know anyone who narrated them from Salim, from Ibn Umar, except Uthman ibn Abd al-Malik."
"6099","Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-Aqadi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Ata' narrated to us: Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to me, from Salim, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your smiling in the face of your brother is recorded for you as charity, and your pouring from your bucket into your brother's bucket is recorded for you as charity."
"6100","And with the same chain he said: Your enjoining good and forbidding evil is recorded for you as charity, your removing harm from the road is recorded for you as charity, and your guiding one who is lost is recorded for you as charity. We do not know anyone who narrated these two hadiths from Ikrimah except Yahya, and we do not know these words narrated from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), through any chain except this one. Yahya ibn Abi Ata' is lenient in hadith; only what he alone narrates is written down from his hadith, with the defect on account of which it was written being made clear."
"6101","Hawtharah ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us: Atiyyah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden. This hadith - we have not heard anyone narrate it except Hawtharah, from Hammad ibn Mas'adah, and we do not know anyone who raised it (to the Prophet) besides him; rather, they narrate it from Hammad, from Ikrimah, from Salim, from his father, as stopped (at Ibn Umar)."
"6102","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Jabir, from Salim, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he travelled, would pray two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, and when he stayed in a land he would perform voluntary prayers."
"6103","Ubaydullah narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Jabir, from Salim and Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Ka'bah with Uthman ibn Shaybah and Bilal, and they closed the door. I was a strong man, so I pushed through until I reached the door, and I found that he had come out. I asked them what he had done, and they said: He prayed two rak'ahs between the two columns."
"6104","Muhammad narrated to us: Ubaydullah narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Jabir, from Salim and Nafi', from Ibn Umar."
"6105","Ahmad ibn Abdah also narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come to Quba riding and walking."
"6106","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Nashit, from Jamil ibn Umarah, from Salim, who said: I heard my father saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, while holding the hand of Ali: Whomever I am his mawla (guardian/master), then this one (Ali) is his mawla. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and oppose whoever opposes him. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Ibn Umar except through this chain, and Jamil ibn Umarah - we do not know anyone who narrated from him except Isma'il ibn Nashit, and we do not know that he narrated from Salim anything except this hadith."
"6107","al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us: Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah: Salim narrated to me, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on a day of Eid and prayed without adhan and without iqamah. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Salim, from his father, except through this chain, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Salim except al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah, and al-Fadl did not narrate from Salim anything other than this hadith."
"6108","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us: Umar ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, will fold the heavens and take them in His right hand, and will fold the earth and take it in His other hand, then He will say: I am the King - where are the kings?"
"6109","Umar ibn Hamzah said: I narrated it to Ikrimah, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said ... then he mentioned something like the hadith of Salim, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"6110","al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj: Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: We used to pledge allegiance to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to hear and obey, and he would say to us: as much as you are able. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Jurayj except Hajjaj, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Musa ibn Uqbah except Ibn Jurayj."
"6111","Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to me, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: This world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Ibn Umar except through the narration of Abdullah ibn Dinar and Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar. As for the hadith of Abdullah ibn Dinar, we do not know anyone who narrated it from him except Musa ibn Uqbah. As for the hadith of Zayd ibn Aslam, Kathir ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar."
"6112","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawahiri narrated to us: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the removal of Your blessing, the shifting of Your protection, the suddenness of Your punishment, and all of Your anger. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with this wording except Abdullah ibn Dinar, nor from Abdullah except Musa ibn Uqbah, nor from Musa except Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"6113","Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6114","Ubayd ibn Isma'il also narrated it to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6115","Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated it to us: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He forbade selling wala' (the tie of clientage) and giving it as a gift. Muhammad ibn Ubayd added in his hadith: from Sufyan, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Wala' belongs to the one who frees. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sufyan except Muhammad ibn Ubayd."
"6116","Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated it to us: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"6117","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated it to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"6118","Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray on his mount wherever it took him while travelling."
"6119","Muhammad narrated to us: Isma'il narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah forgive Ghifar, may Allah grant peace to Aslam, and Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"6120","Nasr ibn Ali narrated it to us: Abu Ahmad informed us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the same."
"6121","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Ahmad informed us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by al-Hijr, he said: Do not enter the dwellings of these punished people unless you are weeping; do not enter upon them lest there befall you what befell them."
"6122","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Ahmad narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: We disliked speaking during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), fearing that the Qur'an would be revealed concerning us; when he passed away, we spoke."
"6123","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come to the mosque of Quba every Saturday, coming to it walking and riding."
"6124","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever keeps a dog, except a dog for herding livestock or a hunting dog, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day."
"6125","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When a Jew greets you, he only says: al-sam (death) be upon you, so say: and upon you."
"6126","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah also narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Jews greet you, they say: al-sam be upon you, so say: and upon you."
"6127","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Ahmad informed us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pointed with his hand toward the east and said: Tribulation is here - or from here - from where the horn of Satan rises."
"6128","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us: Ubaydullah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every two parties to a sale - there is no concluded sale between them until they part, except a sale with the option (to cancel)."
"6129","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated it to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"6130","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Ubayd ibn Waqid al-Qaysi narrated to us: Abu Mudar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: Hatim was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: That is a man who sought a matter and attained it."
"6131","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Nafi' ibn Yazid narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid Yazid ibn al-Had narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the gravest of lies is one who claims (descent) to other than his father, among the gravest of lies is one who claims his eyes saw in a dream what they did not see, and among the gravest of lies is one who says about me what I did not say."
"6132","Umar ibn al-Khattab and Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad both narrated to us, saying: Qutbah ibn al-Ala' ibn al-Minhal narrated to us: Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two ravenous wolves in an enclosure, eating and spoiling, are no more harmful in it than love of honour and love of wealth are to the religion of a Muslim man. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Ibn Umar except through this chain, nor from Abdullah ibn Dinar except by al-Thawri, nor from al-Thawri except by Qutbah ibn al-Ala'."
"6133","Ubaydullah ibn al-Jahm al-Anmati narrated to us: Damrah ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever owns a relative whom it is forbidden to marry is free."
"6134","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Buhlul ibn Muwarriq narrated to us: Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: Abu Bakr - may Allah have mercy on him - brought Abu Quhafah, leading him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a blind old man on the day of the conquest of Makkah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not leave the old man until we came to him? He said: I wanted, O Messenger of Allah, that Allah reward him. By the One who sent you with the truth, my joy at the Islam of Abu Talib would have been greater than my joy at the Islam of my own father, seeking thereby the delight of your eye. He said: You have spoken the truth. This hadith - we do not know it narrated with this wording except through this chain; Musa ibn Ubaydah is one of the worshippers, and he was not a memorizer of hadith because he was preoccupied with worship, as we see - and Allah knows best."
"6135","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Buhlul narrated to us: Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar marriage, the sale of bajar, the sale involving uncertainty (gharar), the sale of a debt for a debt, and the sale of something prompt for something deferred. He said: Bajar is what is in the wombs; gharar is selling what you do not have; debt for debt is a debt in exchange for a debt; prompt for deferred is when you are owed a thousand dirhams by a man, and a man says: I will pay you five hundred promptly and leave the rest; and shighar is marrying a woman in exchange for a woman with no dower for either."
"6136","al-Walid ibn Amr ibn Sukayn narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us: Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The poor believers complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the preference given to their rich brothers, saying: O Messenger of Allah, our brothers affirm as we affirm, believe as we believe, fast as we fast, yet they have wealth from which they give charity, maintain kinship ties, and spend in the path of Allah, while we are poor and cannot do that. He said: Shall I not tell you something which, if you do it, you will attain the same merit as them? Say: Allahu Akbar (Allah is greatest) after every prayer eleven times, al-hamdu lillah (praise be to Allah) likewise, la ilaha illa Allah (there is no god but Allah) likewise, and subhan Allah (glory be to Allah) likewise - you will attain the same merit as them. They did so, then they mentioned it to the rich, who did the same. The poor returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, saying: These brothers of ours have done the same as we say. He said: That is the bounty of Allah which He gives to whom He wills. O company of the poor, shall I not give you glad tidings? The poor Muslims will enter Paradise half a day - five hundred years - before their rich. And Musa ibn Ubaydah recited: {And indeed a day with your Lord is like a thousand years of what you count}. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Ibn Umar except through this chain, and we have already mentioned Musa ibn Ubaydah."
"6137","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Buhlul narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah: Sadaqah ibn Yasar and Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to me, from Ibn Umar."
"6138","al-Walid ibn Amr ibn Sukayn also narrated to us: Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us: Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar and Sadaqah ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, who said: This surah, {When the help of Allah comes and the victory}, was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina while he was in the middle of the days of tashriq during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he knew it was the farewell. He ordered his camel al-Qaswa', and it was saddled for him; then he rode and stood before the people at al-Aqabah, and as many Muslims as Allah willed gathered to him. He praised Allah and glorified Him as He deserves, then said: To proceed, O people: every blood (claim) that existed in the pre-Islamic age is void, and the first of your blood (claims) that I void is the blood of Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith, who was being suckled among Banu Layth when Hudhayl killed him. Every usury that existed in the pre-Islamic age is abolished, and the first of your usury that I abolish is the usury of al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib. O people, time has turned to its original state on the day Allah created the heavens and the earth; the number of months with Allah is twelve months, of which four are sacred: Rajab of Mudar, which is between Jumada and Sha'ban, Dhu al-Qa'dah, Dhu al-Hijjah, and al-Muharram. That is the upright religion, so do not wrong yourselves in them. {Postponement (of sacred months) is an increase in disbelief by which the disbelievers are led astray; they make it lawful one year and forbid it one year to adjust the number of what Allah has forbidden}. They would make Safar lawful one year and forbid al-Muharram one year, and forbid Safar one year and make al-Muharram lawful one year - that is the postponement. O people, whoever has a trust with him, let him return it to the one who entrusted him with it. O people, Satan has despaired of being worshipped in your lands at the end of time, but he is content with despised deeds among you, so beware for your religion regarding despised deeds. O people, women are captives with you; you took them in the trust of Allah and made their private parts lawful by the word of Allah. You have rights over them and they have rights over you; part of your rights over them is that they not allow anyone other than you on your beds, and that they not disobey you in what is right. If they do that, then you have no (further) way against them; they are entitled to their provision and clothing in a reasonable manner. If you strike, then strike without severity. It is not lawful for a man to take anything of his brother's wealth except what he willingly gives. O people, I have left among you that which, if you hold to it, you will not go astray: the Book of Allah - so act upon it. O people, what day is this? They said: A sacred day. He said: What land is this? They said: A sacred land. He said: What month is this? They said: A sacred month. He said: Allah, blessed and exalted, has made your blood, your wealth, and your honour sacred like the sanctity of this day, this month, and this land. Let your present convey to your absent; there is no prophet after me, and no community after you. Then he raised his hands and said: O Allah, bear witness."
"6139","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Humayd ibn Hammad ibn Abi al-Khawar narrated to me: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which people recite best? He said: The one whom, when you hear him reciting, you see that he fears Allah. This hadith - we do not know anyone who corroborated Humayd ibn Hammad in his narration; Mis'ar only narrates it from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, as mursal. Mis'ar did not narrate anything from Abdullah ibn Dinar, and we heard this hadith only from Muhammad ibn Ma'mar, who produced it for us from his book."
"6140","Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The noble one, son of the noble one, son of the noble one, son of the noble one - Yusuf ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, peace be upon them. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Ibn Umar except through this chain, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abdullah ibn Dinar except his son Abd al-Rahman; Abd al-Rahman is lenient in hadith, though a group of scholars narrated from him and accepted his hadith."
"6141","Ali ibn Harb narrated to us: Yahya ibn al-Yaman narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked briskly (ramal) from one corner (of the Ka'bah) to the other."
"6142","Ishaq ibn Hatim al-Allaf narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us: Imran ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who remembers Allah among the heedless is like one who fights alongside those who flee."
"6143","Ahmad ibn Abdah and Ishaq ibn Hatim both narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us: Imran ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says in any marketplace: There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner to Him; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise; He gives life and causes death, and He is the Living who does not die; in His hand is good, and He is capable of all things - if he says it once, Allah records for him a million good deeds, erases from him a million bad deeds, and builds for him a house in Paradise."
"6144","Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Darir al-Wasiti narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When my community walks with swagger and the sons of Persia and Rome serve them - their enemy will be given power over them. Or words like these. This hadith is only narrated by Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Yunus: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ... and no one is known to have corroborated Muhammad Isma'il in this narration from Abu Mu'awiyah."
"6145","This hadith is only known through the hadith of Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah."
"6146","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Nafi' narrated to us: Asim ibn Umar al-Umari narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first for whom the earth will split open on the Day of Resurrection, then Abu Bakr, then Umar; then I will come to al-Baqi' and they will be gathered with me, then I will wait for the people of Makkah until I am gathered between the two sanctuaries - or between the people of the two sanctuaries."
"6147","Amr ibn Abd al-Rahman, son of the daughter of Hammad ibn Mas'adah, narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Nafi' narrated to us: Asim ibn Umar narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ramadan in Makkah is better than a thousand Ramadans elsewhere than Makkah. The two hadiths of Asim ibn Umar - we do not know anyone who narrated them besides him, and we do not know their words narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain."
"6148","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sadaqah. And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed Dhu al-Hulayfah as the miqat for the people of Madinah, al-Juhfah for the people of Syria, and Qarn for the people of Najd."
"6149","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us: al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to me: Sadaqah ibn Yasar narrated to me, saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays, let him pray toward a sutrah (barrier), and let him not allow anyone to pass in front of him; if he refuses, then let him fight him, for with him is the qarin - meaning Satan."
"6150","Uqbah ibn Mukram and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar both narrated to us, saying: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Yasar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a chamber in the mosque where he would seclude himself (i'tikaf) in the last part of Ramadan, and he would pray in it. He put his head out of it and said: A person praying converses privately with his Lord, so let each of you consider what he converses with Him about, and let not some of you raise their voices over others. This hadith - we do not know it narrated except from Ibn Umar, and we do not know any chain from Ibn Umar except this one."
"6151","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us: Bistam ibn Hurayth and Sadaqah ibn Yasar narrated to us, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba' (pumpkin vessels), hantam (green jars), and muzaffat (pitched vessels). This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it except Affan, and we do not know it narrated from Sadaqah ibn Yasar except through this chain. Muharib ibn Dithar narrated it from Ibn Umar; al-Zuhri narrated it from Salim; Mujahid narrated it from Ibn Umar; and others narrated it from Ibn Umar. As for the hadith of Muharib:"
"6152","Muhammad ibn Isma'il narrated it to us, from Asbat, from al-Shaybani, from Muharib, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6153","al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us: Shabababah ibn Sawwar narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the hypocrite - or he said: the example of the Muslim - is like a green tree. He said: And I thought it was the date-palm, so I wanted to say it, but I was young and felt shy. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is the date-palm. Ibn Umar said: I told my father what I had wanted to say, and he said: Had you said it, it would have been dearer to me than such-and-such."
"6154","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us: Khubayb narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Ibn Umar: that he travelled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he prayed at Mina the traveler's prayer, and with Abu Bakr the traveler's prayer, and with Umar the traveler's prayer, and with Uthman the traveler's prayer; then afterwards he (Uthman) prayed four."
"6155","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far al-Madani, who said: I heard Abu al-Muthanna narrating from Ibn Umar, who said: The adhan during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in pairs, and the iqamah once, except that the caller would say: qad qamat al-salah (prayer has begun) - twice."
"6156","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Budayl ibn Maysarah and Ayyub, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Umar."
"6157","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik also narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Abu Mijlaz, from Ibn Umar."
"6158","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi narrated to us: Marhum ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Attar narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - while I was between him and the questioner - about the night prayer. He said: Two by two; when you sense, or fear, the morning, make the last of your prayer witr (odd). This hadith has been narrated from Ibn Umar through several chains with different wordings, but the meaning is one or close."
"6159","al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Habib narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Enjoy this House (the Ka'bah), for it has been demolished twice and will be raised on the third. This hadith - we heard no one narrate it except al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah, from Sufyan ibn Habib; it has been narrated from Hammad, from Humayd, from Bakr, from Ibn Umar, as stopped."
"6160","al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Jazari narrated to us: Sahl ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Bakr, from Ibn Umar, who said: It is from the Sunnah that a man bathe when he intends to enter ihram. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Ibn Umar through any chain better than this one."
"6161","Isma'il ibn Mas'ud narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Bakr, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah together, so I mentioned that to Ibn Umar, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only entered ihram for Hajj."
"6162","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Sahl ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Bakr, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: Anas narrated to us that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Labbayk for Umrah and Hajj. He said: Woe to Anas! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and called the talbiyah for Hajj, and we called it with him. When he arrived, he ordered whoever did not have a sacrificial animal with him to make it Umrah. I mentioned that to Anas, and he said: You count us as nothing but children."
"6163","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Bakr."
"6164","Amr ibn Yazid Abu Burayd narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani."
"6165","Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Zakariyya al-Ghassani narrated to us: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Abdullah - the wording being the wording of Humayd - that he used to say: Labbayk Allahumma labbayk; labbayk, no partner have You, labbayk; indeed praise, blessing, and dominion are Yours; no partner have You. And it is mentioned as from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6166","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abd al-A'la narrated to us: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Yunus ibn Jubayr Abu Ghallab, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about a man who divorces his wife while she is menstruating. He said: Do you know Abdullah ibn Umar? He divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so Umar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered him to take her back. I said: Is that menstruation counted? He said: Be quiet - what if he were incapable and foolish?"
"6167","Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. We do not know that Yunus ibn Jubayr narrated from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), anything other than this hadith."
"6168","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muslim al-Qurri, who said: I was with Ibn Umar when a man came to him and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what about witr - is it Sunnah? He said: It is Sunnah; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed witr and the Muslims prayed witr. We do not know that Muslim al-Qurri narrated from Ibn Umar anything except this hadith; he is a man from Basra."
"6169","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us: Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Ibn Umar, who said: A man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which part of the night is most responsive? He said: The last part of the night. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Ibn Umar except through this chain, and we do not know that Abu Qilabah narrated from Ibn Umar anything except this hadith."
"6170","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us: Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, who said: When Ibn Umar went to his bed, he would say: O Allah, You created my soul and You take it; to You belong its death and its life. O Allah, if You take it, forgive it, and if You return it, protect it. O Allah, I ask You for well-being. A man from his offspring said: Did Ibn Umar say this? He said: Rather, one better than Ibn Umar used to say this. We do not know that Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated from Ibn Umar anything other than this hadith; Abdullah ibn al-Harith is al-Sirini."
"6171","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali both narrated to us, saying: Umar ibn Abi Khalifah narrated to us: Ziyad ibn Mikhraq narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Mu'adh and Abu Musa, saying: Consult one another and agree, make things easy and do not make them hard, give glad tidings and do not drive people away. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Ibn Umar except through this chain."
"6172","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Tawbah al-Anbari, from Mawraq al-Ijli: I said to Ibn Umar: Do you pray Duha? He said: No. I said: Did Umar pray it? He said: No. I said: Did Abu Bakr pray it? He said: No. I said: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray it? He said: I do not think he prayed it."
"6173","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Ali ibn Abdullah al-Bariqi: that a woman asked Ibn Umar about silk, and he said: We used to say that whoever wears it in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter. We do not know that Qatadah narrated from Ali ibn Abdullah anything other than this hadith."
"6174","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Ya'qub, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Nu'm narrating, saying: I witnessed Ibn Umar when a man asked him about a pilgrim in ihram killing flies. He said: O people of Iraq, you ask me about killing flies when you killed the son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They (al-Hasan and al-Husayn) are my two sweet basils in this world - meaning al-Hasan and al-Husayn."
"6175","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: We were with Ibn Sirin, and al-Mughirah ibn Salman was there. Al-Mughirah narrated from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray two rak'ahs before Zuhr and two after it, two after Maghrib, two after Isha, and two after Fajr. We do not know that al-Mughirah ibn Salman narrated from Ibn Umar anything other than this hadith."
"6176","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Baylamani narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {Every day He is engaged in some matter} - He said: He forgives a sin and removes distress."
"6177","Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Dimashqi narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to me: Hafs ibn Ghaylan narrated to me, from Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, who said: We were with Ibn Umar at Mina when a young man from Basra came asking him about something. He said: I will tell you about that. I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as one of ten in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Ibn Mas'ud, Mu'adh, Hudhayfah, Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, another man whom he named, and myself. A young man from the Ansar came to him, greeted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then sat and said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the believers is best? He said: The best of them in character. He said: Which of the believers is wisest? He said: Those who remember death most and prepare best for it before it befalls them - or he said: befalls him - those are the wise. Then the young man fell silent, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to us and said: Immorality never appears among a people but plague and ailments that never occurred among their predecessors appear among them; they never give short measure and weight but they are seized by years (of drought), severe hardship, and the tyranny of the ruler over them; they never withhold the zakah of their wealth but rain from the sky is withheld from them - were it not for the animals they would receive no rain; they never break the covenant of Allah and His Messenger but their enemy is given power over them and takes some of what was in their hands; and when their leaders do not judge by the Book of Allah, Allah sets their strife among themselves. He said: Then he ordered Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf to prepare for an expedition over which he appointed him. In the morning he had wrapped himself in a turban of black coarse cloth, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him, undid it, turbaned him himself, letting four fingers hang from behind, then said: This is how, O Ibn Awf, wrap your turban, for it is more dignified and better. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal to hand him the banner. He praised Allah, then said: Go forth all together in the path of Allah; fight those who disbelieve in Allah; do not steal from the spoils, do not betray, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child. This is the covenant of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his practice among you."
"6178","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about vows, and he said: A vow neither brings anything forward nor delays it, but something is extracted by it from the miser."
"6179","Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Arhabi narrated to us: Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from Sinan ibn al-Harith, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque at Mina when a man from the Ansar and a man from Thaqif came to him. They greeted him, then said: O Messenger of Allah, we have come to ask you. He said: If you wish, I will tell you what you came to ask me about, and if you wish, I will hold back and you may ask me. They said: Tell us, O Messenger of Allah. The Thaqafi said to the Ansari: Ask. He said: Tell me, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You came to ask me about your leaving your house heading for the Sacred House and what you have in it, about your two rak'ahs after circumambulation and what you have in them, about your going between al-Safa and al-Marwah and what you have in it, your standing on the evening of Arafah and what you have in it, your stoning the pillars and what you have in it, your sacrifice and what you have in it, your shaving your head and what you have in it, and your circumambulation of the House after that along with the farewell and what you have in it. He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, this is what I came to ask you about. He said: When you leave your house heading for the Sacred House, your camel does not place its foot nor lift it but Allah records for you a good deed thereby and erases from you a sin. As for your two rak'ahs after circumambulation, they are like freeing a slave from the children of Isma'il. As for your going between al-Safa and al-Marwah after that, it is like freeing seventy slaves. As for your standing on the evening of Arafah, Allah, blessed and exalted, descends to the lowest heaven and boasts of you to the angels, saying: My servants have come to Me dishevelled from every deep mountain pass, hoping for My mercy; even if your sins were as numerous as sand, drops of rain, or the foam of the sea, He would forgive them - Depart, My servants, forgiven are you and those for whom you intercede. As for your stoning the pillars, for every pebble you throw you have (the expiation of) a grave destructive sin. As for your sacrifice, it is stored for you with your Lord. As for your shaving your head, for every hair you shave you have a good deed and a sin is erased from you thereby. As for your circumambulation of the House after that, you circumambulate with no sin upon you; an angel comes and places his hands between your shoulders, saying: Act concerning what is to come, for what has passed has been forgiven. These words have been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through several chains, and we know of no chain better than this one. Attaf ibn Khalid narrated these words from Isma'il ibn Rafi', from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); the hadith of Ibn Umar is similar."
"6180","Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us: Ali ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us: Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: Some women of the Ansar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O women of the Ansar, dye (with henna) in five ways, circumcise lightly and do not go to excess, for it is more pleasing to your husbands; and beware of ingratitude to benefactors. Mindal said: meaning husbands. End of the musnad of Ibn Umar, and praise be to Allah."
"6181","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman: that Abu Talhah prepared food for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sent Anas ibn Malik. He came until he entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among his Companions. He said: Did your father invite us? He said: Yes. He said: Arise. Anas said: I went to Abu Talhah and told him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, it is only food we wanted to present to you as a gift. He called for it, placed his hand upon it, and invoked blessing. He said: Admit ten. He admitted them and they ate until they were full. Then he said: Admit ten. He admitted them, and I kept admitting ten by ten until all of them were full, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left over for us as much as we had prepared, or more."
"6182","Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated it to us: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. We do not know that Muhammad ibn Ka'b narrated from Anas anything other than this hadith, nor do we know anything authentic from Abu Salamah from Anas other than this hadith, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr except Abu Usamah."
"6183","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leaders are from Quraysh as long as they act upon three things: when mercy is sought from them they show mercy, when they make a covenant they fulfil it, and when they judge they are just. We do not know that Sa'd ibn Ibrahim narrated from Anas anything except this hadith."
"6184","Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us: Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Abi Dharrah, from Ja'far ibn Amr ibn Umayyah al-Damri, from Anas."
"6185","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim al-Juddi narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawali: Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr, from Ja'far ibn Amr ibn Umayyah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever Allah grants forty years of life in Islam, Allah averts from him various kinds of affliction: madness, leprosy, and vitiligo - Abd al-Malik al-Juddi said in his hadith: Allah holds back from him various kinds of affliction: leprosy, vitiligo, and the strangling of Satan - Whoever Allah grants fifty years of life in Islam, Allah makes the reckoning easy for him - Abu Damrah said: Allah makes the reckoning easy for him on the Day of Resurrection - Whoever Allah grants sixty years of life in Islam, Allah grants him turning to Him in what Allah loves - Abu Damrah said: Allah grants him good turning to Him - Whoever Allah grants seventy years of life in Islam, the inhabitants of heaven and earth love him. Whoever Allah grants eighty years of life in Islam, Allah erases his bad deeds and records his good deeds - Anas ibn Iyad said in his hadith: his good deeds are recorded and his bad deeds are not recorded - Whoever Allah grants ninety years of life in Islam, Allah forgives his sins, he becomes Allah's captive on His earth, and an intercessor for his household on the Day of Resurrection - Anas ibn Iyad said: he is Allah's captive on His earth, and intercession is granted for his household. We do not know that Ja'far ibn Amr ibn Umayyah narrated from Anas anything except this hadith."
"6186","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of the hypocrite is that he sits waiting for the sun until, when it has yellowed and is upon the two horns of Satan, or between the two horns of Satan, he stands and pecks four (rak'ahs), remembering Allah only a little."
"6187","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us: Malik narrated to us, from al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub, who said: We visited Anas ibn Malik after Zuhr, and he stood to pray Asr. When he finished his prayer, we said to him: Are you hastening the prayer? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: That is the prayer of the hypocrites, that is the prayer of the hypocrites, that is the prayer of the hypocrites: one of them sits until, when the sun has yellowed and is between the two horns of Satan, or upon the two horns of Satan, he stands and pecks four, remembering Allah in them only a little. We do not know that al-Ala' ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated from Anas anything except this hadith."
"6188","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu Amir narrated to us: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik, who informed him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray Friday prayer when the sun declined, and when he went out to Makkah he would pray Zuhr at al-Shajarah as two rak'ahs."
"6189","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu Amir al-Aqadi Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Ja'far - meaning al-Mukharrami - from the descendants of al-Miswar ibn Makhramah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to the people while they were praying sitting due to illness, and said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing. We do not know these words narrated from Anas except through this chain, apart from a hadith in which Ibn Jurayj errs, narrating it from al-Zuhri, from Anas. We do not know that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd narrated from Anas anything except this hadith."
"6190","Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering a sermon one day, a man entered through a door facing the pulpit and said: O Messenger of Allah - peace be upon him - wealth has perished and roads are cut off, so ask Allah to relieve us. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands and said: O Allah, give us rain; O Allah, give us rain; O Allah, give us rain. By Allah, no cloud or wisp was seen in the sky, nor was there any house or dwelling between us and Sal' (mountain). A cloud like a shield rose from its corner; when it reached the middle of the sky, it spread. Anas said: By Allah, we did not see the sun for six days. Then a man came through that same door on the following Friday while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon standing. When he faced him standing, he said: O Messenger of Allah, wealth has perished and roads are cut off, so ask Allah to remove it from us. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands and said: O Allah, around us and not upon us; O Allah, upon the hills, the mounds, the bottoms of valleys, and the places where trees grow. He said: It cleared, and we went out walking in the sunshine. Sharik said: I asked Anas: Is he the first man? He said: I do not know."
"6191","Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us: Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us: Sharik ibn Abi Namir narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik."
"6192","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar also narrated it to us: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abdullah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and warned the people. A man stood and said: When is the Hour, O Messenger of Allah? We said to him: Sit down, for you have asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about something he dislikes. Then he stood a second time and said: When is the Hour? Disapproval appeared on the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than the first time - meaning dislike. He said: We seated him. Then he stood a third time and said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: Woe to you - what have you prepared for it? The man said: I have prepared for it love of Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sit, for you are with those you love."
"6193","Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us: Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abdullah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I never prayed behind an imam whose prayer was lighter than that of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor more complete; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would hear a child crying behind him and lighten (the prayer) for fear that his mother would be distressed."
"6194","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to me, from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I heard him saying: While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque, a man entered upon a camel, made it kneel in the mosque, then said to them: Which of you is Muhammad? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was reclining among them. He said: We said: He is the fair man reclining. The man said: I adjure you by your Lord and the Lord of those before you - has Allah sent you to all people? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah - has Allah commanded you to pray the five prayers in the day and night? He said: O Allah, yes. He said: I adjure you by Allah - has Allah commanded you to take this charity from our rich and distribute it among our poor? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, yes. The man said: I believe in what you have brought, and I am the messenger of those behind me from my people; I am Dimam ibn Tha'labah, brother of Banu Sa'd ibn Bakr. This hadith - we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, nor from Sharik from Anas except by Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, nor from Sa'id except by al-Layth."
"6195","al-Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ammar, a Madinan, narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is the mirror of the believer. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sharik except Muhammad ibn Ammar, and we do not know it narrated from Anas except through this chain."
"6196","And with the same chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out when the prayer was established and saw people praying the two rak'ahs of Fajr. He said: Two prayers together? And he forbade praying them when the prayer has been established. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Anas except through this chain with this isnad. Muhammad ibn Ammar was the caller to prayer of the mosque of Quba; Abu Amir al-Aqadi, Bishr ibn Umar, and others narrated from him."
"6197","al-Sakan ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Husayn ibn Ata' narrated to me, from Dawud ibn Bakr, from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought rain before the prayer, faced the qiblah, turned his cloak, then came down and prayed two rak'ahs. This hadith contradicts what was narrated from Abdullah ibn Yazid and from Abu Hurayrah. We do not know it narrated from Anas except through this chain."
"6198","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, as I believe: Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The martyrs are three: A man who goes out with his life and wealth, seeking reward in the path of Allah, not intending to kill, nor to be killed, nor to fight, increasing the numbers of the Muslims; if he dies or is killed, all his sins are forgiven, he is protected from the punishment of the grave, secured from the greatest terror, married to the wide-eyed maidens, clothed in the garment of honour, and a crown of dignity and eternity is placed upon his head. The second: a man who goes out with his life and wealth, seeking reward, intending to be killed but not to kill; if he dies or is killed, his knee will be with the knee of Ibrahim, the close friend of the Merciful, before Allah, blessed and exalted, in a seat of truth with a most powerful King. The third: a man who goes out with his life and wealth, seeking reward, intending to kill and to be killed; if he dies or is killed, he will come on the Day of Resurrection with his sword unsheathed, placed upon his shoulder, while the people kneel on their knees, saying: Make way for us, for we offered our blood for Allah, blessed and exalted. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, if he were to say to Ibrahim, the close friend of the Merciful, or to any prophet among the prophets, they would move aside from the path for him because of what he sees of their due right, until they come to pulpits of light to the right of the Throne. They will sit upon them, watching how judgement is passed among the people; they will not feel the pangs of death, nor remain in the barzakh, nor will the Blast frighten them, nor will the reckoning, the balance, or the bridge concern them. They will watch how judgement is passed among the people; they will ask for nothing but it will be given to them, and they will intercede for nothing but their intercession will be accepted for it. They will be given of Paradise whatever they love, settling in Paradise wherever they love. This hadith - we do not know it narrated except from Anas through this chain; Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah narrated hadiths that were not corroborated, and I think this hadith came from him only, for Muslim ibn Khalid was not a memorizer."
"6199","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Qays narrated to us: I heard Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman mentioning from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent at the age of forty; he stayed in Makkah ten years and in Madinah ten years, and died at the age of sixty, with not twenty white hairs on his head and beard. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither conspicuously tall nor short, neither stark white nor dark, neither very curly-haired nor lank-haired."
"6200","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither white nor dark, neither tall nor short, nor curly-haired. Revelation came to him when he was forty years old; he stayed in Makkah ten years and in Madinah ten years, and died - peace be upon him - at sixty years of age; when he died, there were not twenty white hairs on his head. This hadith has been narrated from Rabi'ah by a group, so we have limited ourselves to those we named."
"6201","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us: Marwan ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the head of al-Hasan or al-Husayn to be shaved on the seventh day, and that silver equal to its weight be given in charity."
"6202","Safwan ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us: Mujja'ah ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Rabi'ah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"6203","Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari. And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he had relieved himself, he stood at the side of the mosque and urinated in it. The people shouted at him, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) restrained the people from him, then ordered a bucket of water which was poured over his urine."
"6204","Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not tell you of the best quarters of the Ansar? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The best quarters of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar. We said: Then which? He said: Then the quarters of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, then the quarters of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu Sa'idah. Then he gestured with his hand, turning it over them, then said: Every quarter of the Ansar is good. These two hadiths have been narrated from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas, by a group."
"6205","Khallad ibn Aslam narrated to us: Hanifah ibn Marzuq narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muhaqalah - I think he said: and muzabanah - and permitted araya (sales)."
"6206","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us: Mu'alla ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never shook hands with anyone and parted from him until the man was the one who parted from him."
"6207","Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us: Mu'alla ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid. And Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated it to us: al-Walid ibn Ata' ibn al-Agharr narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman narrated to us - both from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not raise his hands in any supplication except in seeking rain. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id except Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far and Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman. Mu'alla ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated from Abd al-Hamid hadiths upon which he was not corroborated, and we do not know anyone who narrated the hadith of Yahya from Anas - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never seen parting from a man until the man was the one who parted - except Mu'alla."
"6208","Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Bazzar narrated to us: Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Harithi narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the two leather socks. This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Anas except Ya'qub ibn Isma'il; al-Darawardi narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn Ruqaysh, from Anas."
"6209","Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Ahmad ibn Thabit both narrated to us, saying: Abu Hisham al-Mughirah ibn Salamah narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, give us rain. This hadith has been disputed over from Yahya ibn Sa'id: a group narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather; more than one narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id as mursal."
"6210","Rizqullah ibn Musa narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Dawud al-Mikhraqi narrated to us: Malik narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas, who said: I never prayed behind anyone whose prayer was lighter than that of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Malik except Isma'il ibn Dawud; he was known as al-Mikhraqi because he was the son of Dawud ibn Mikhraq."
"6211","Abdullah ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us: Badal ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In every quarter of the Ansar there is good."
"6212","al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id and Rabi'ah, from Anas, who said: There were not twenty white hairs on the head and beard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6213","Abu al-Rabi' al-Harithi Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: Isa ibn Abi Isa informed me, from Abu al-Zinad, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Envy consumes good deeds as fire consumes firewood, charity extinguishes sin as water extinguishes fire, prayer is the light of the believer, and fasting is a shield from the Fire. We do not know that Abu al-Zinad narrated from Anas anything except this hadith. Abu Bakr said: They are three separate hadiths, and I have joined them."
"6214","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Samurah narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Sa'id, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: Abu Talhah sent me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to invite him to a khazirah (a dish). I came to him while he was with his Companions; when I drew near him, he said: Has Abu Talhah invited us? I said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arose, and those of his Companions who were with him arose. Food was brought - meaning the dish - and he invoked blessing in it. He said: Call some men for me. He called ten or so, and they ate from it until they were full, then they went out; another ten entered and ate until they were full. All those who were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate until they were full. I looked at its remainder, and it was as it was - meaning before - and he said: You have this with you, so fulfil your needs from it. I know of no one who narrated from Sa'd ibn Sa'id except through this chain; Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi and Abu Usamah narrated it from Sa'd."
"6215","al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us: Yahya ibn al-Yaman narrated to us: Yasin ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This community will split into seventy-odd sects; I know the best guided among them. They said: Which is it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The congregation (al-jama'ah). This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Anas except through another narration of Sa'd ibn Sa'id, Yahya ibn Sa'id; we do not know anyone who narrated it from him except Yasin ibn Mu'adh, called Yasin al-Zayyat. He was not strong."
"6216","Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Uqbah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Sa'd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, saying: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O company of the Ansar, your appointed meeting with me is my Hawd (pool); its vessels are more numerous than the stars of the sky, or like the number of the stars of the sky, and its width is like the distance between me and San'a', or like the distance between me and Oman. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Sa'd ibn Sa'id from Anas except through this chain."
"6217","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Hour will not come until time draws near, so a year becomes like a month, a month like a week, a week like a day, a day like an hour, and an hour like the burning of a palm leaf with fire. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Anas except through the hadith of Sa'd ibn Sa'id; Abdullah ibn Umar alone narrated it from Sa'd."
"6218","Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us: Mutarrif ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever sees an afflicted person and says: Praise be to Allah who has spared me from what He has afflicted you with - he will be spared that affliction."
"6219","Abdullah ibn Shabib also narrated it to us: Mutarrif ibn Abdullah and Ishaq al-Farwi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Abd Rabbihi ibn Sa'id, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. We do not know that Abd Rabbihi narrated from Anas anything except this hadith."
"6220","Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Hakam al-Warraq narrated to us: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rewards of my community were shown to me, even the speck of dirt a man removes from the mosque, and the sins of my community were shown to me, and I saw no sin greater than a surah of the Qur'an, or a verse of the Qur'an - I think he said: which one learns then forgets. We do not know that al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab narrated from Anas anything except this hadith, nor that anyone narrated it from Ibn Jurayj except Abd al-Majid."
"6221","Ziyad ibn Yahya Abu al-Khattab narrated to us: Abd al-Wahhab, meaning Ibn Abd al-Majid, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Khunays, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: Love of Allah and His Messenger. He said: Then you are with those you love. We do not know that Kathir ibn Khunays narrated from Anas anything except this hadith."
"6222","Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us: Sa'id ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us: Musa ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Abu al-Huwayrith narrated to me: Nu'aym ibn Abdullah al-Mujmir narrated to me, that Anas ibn Malik informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things - whoever has them has tasted the flavour of faith: one for whom nothing is dearer than Allah and His Messenger, one for whom being burned with fire is dearer than abandoning his religion, and one who loves for Allah and hates for Allah. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Anas through any chain better than this one, and we do not know that Nu'aym al-Mujmir narrated from Anas anything except this hadith. The name of Abu al-Huwayrith is Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah, a well-known man from Madinah."
"6223","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Bakr ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Abu Tuwalah, from Anas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I love you. He said: Then prepare for poverty."
"6224","Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar both narrated to us - the wording being that of Ibn Ma'mar - saying: Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Hawiyyah ibn Ubayd, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Adam will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and it will be said to him: Intercede. He will say: I am not the one for that; go to Nuh, for he is the first of the prophets and the greatest of them. Nuh will be brought and will say: I am not the one for you; go to Ibrahim, for Allah took him as a close friend. Ibrahim will be brought and will say: I am not the one for you; go to Musa, for Allah spoke to him directly. Musa will be brought and will say: I am not the one for you; go to Isa, for he is the spirit of Allah and His word. Isa will be brought and will say: I am not the one for you, but I will guide you to the one for you - go to Muhammad, peace be upon him. He said: I will be brought and will seek to open; when I look at the Most Merciful, I will fall prostrate to Him. I will remain - or he said: I will stay - as long as Allah wills, then it will be said: Raise your head; speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and your intercession will be accepted. I will raise my head and say: O Lord, my community. It will be said: Go - and whoever has the weight of a dinar of faith in his heart, let him leave none of them (in the Fire); thereby as many as Allah wills will come out. Then I will fall prostrate a second time and remain as long as Allah wills me to remain, then it will be said: Raise your head, O Muhammad; speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and your intercession will be accepted. I will raise my head and say: O Lord, my community. It will be said: Go and leave no one in the Fire who has half a dinar of faith in his heart but you bring him out. Thereby as many as Allah wills will come out. Then I will fall prostrate a third time and remain as long as Allah wills, then it will be said: Raise your head, O Muhammad; speak and you will be heard, ask and you will be given, intercede and your intercession will be accepted. I will raise my head and say: O Lord, my community. It will be said: Go and leave no one in the Fire who has the weight of a grain of faith in his heart but you bring him out; thereby as many as Allah wills will come out, and none will remain except one in whom there is no good. Hawiyyah ibn Ubayd is a man from Madinah; we do not know anyone who narrated from him except Ibn Ajlan."
"6225","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu Amir narrated to us: Fulayh, meaning Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not foul-mouthed, nor one who cursed, nor obscene; when admonishing one of us, he would say: What is wrong with him - may his forehead be dusted."
"6226","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: We attended the funeral of a daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting at the grave, and I saw his eyes shedding tears. He said: Is there among you a man who did not commit (an act) last night? Abu Talhah said: I. He said: Then descend. We do not know anyone who narrated these two hadiths except Hilal ibn Ali from Anas with this wording."
"6227","Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us at our house with Abu Bakr, Umar, and some Bedouins. I milked a sheep for them, then water from our well was poured over it, and he drank, with Abu Bakr to his left, Umar facing him, and the Bedouins to his right. Umar spoke, intending (to give to) Abu Bakr, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed it to the Bedouin, saying: Those on the right, those on the right. Anas said: It is Sunnah. Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar is known as Abu Tuwalah."
"6228","Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu Tuwalah, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The excellence of A'ishah over women is like the excellence of tharid (meat broth with bread) over food - or over other food."
"6229","Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Anas: he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicating and seeking refuge with these words: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from anxiety and grief, incapacity and laziness, miserliness and cowardice, the burden of debt, and the domination of men."
"6230","Ali ibn Sahl al-Mada'ini narrated it to us: al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us: Za'idah narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"6231","Nasr ibn Ali narrated it to us: al-Mu'tamir informed us, from his father, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to the hadith of Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Amr ibn Abi Amr is from Madinah, al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful is from Kufah, and Sulayman, father of al-Mu'tamir, is from Basra. We have only gathered them so as not to repeat the hadith of each man when their wordings are the same."
"6232","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Qays narrated to us, saying: I heard Amr ibn Abi Amr narrating from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am not of idle amusement, nor is idle amusement of me. Abu Muhammad, meaning Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Qays, said: I am not of falsehood, nor is falsehood of me. This hadith - we do not know it narrated except from Anas, nor anyone who narrated it from Amr ibn Abi Amr except Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Qays."
"6233","Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr: he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared sacred what is between the two lava plains of Madinah. This hadith is only known from Anas through the hadith of Amr ibn Abi Amr."
"6234","Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Uhud is a mountain that loves us and we love it. This hadith has been narrated from Anas through more than one chain."
"6235","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us: Musa ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A man entered seeking a lost animal in the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May you not find it. This hadith - we do not know it narrated from Anas except through this chain."
"6236","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Musa ibn 'Ubaydah, 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us, saying: Say: O Allah, we seek refuge in You from anxiety and sorrow, and from incapacity and laziness, and from miserliness and cowardice, and from the burden of debt and the domination of the sons of Adam."
"6237","Sa'id ibn Bahr al-Qaratisiyy narrated it to us, Makkiyy ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn Sa'id, from 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar, except that he said: and the domination of men."
"6238","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mufaddal al-Harrani narrated to us, al-Walid ibn al-Muhallab narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Muhriz al-Azdi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us upon his she-camel al-'Adba', which was not slit-eared, and said: O people, it is as if death here is decreed upon other than us, and as if the truth here is obligatory upon other than us, and as if those dead we escort are travellers who will soon return to us; we settle them in their graves and we consume their inheritance, as if you will remain forever after them, having forgotten every admonition and feeling safe from every calamity. Blessed is he whom his own fault distracts from the faults of people, and who humbles himself for Allah without abasement, and spends from wealth he gathered without disobedience, and mixes with the people of understanding and keeps away from the people of doubt and innovation, and whose outward conduct is righteous and who spares people his evil. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording from Anas except through this channel."
"6239","And another weak channel, narrated by Aban ibn Abi 'Ayyash from Anas: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, from Aban."
"6240","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym and Mu'ammal said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas who said: We prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah the Zuhr prayer as four units, and at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two units."
"6241","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr in Madinah as four units, and prayed 'Asr at al-'Aqiq as two units."
"6242","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj who said: I was informed from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, or I was narrated to, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr in Madinah as four units, and prayed 'Asr at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two units, then he spent the night at Dhu al-Hulayfah until morning; when morning came he mounted his she-camel, and when his mount stood upright he raised his voice with the talbiyah."
"6243","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Zuhr prayer in Madinah, then he mentioned something similar."
"6244","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yazid ibn 'Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no orphanhood after puberty. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Anas except with this isnad; and Yazid ibn 'Abd al-Malik is soft in hadith, though a group of scholars narrated from him and tolerated his hadith despite his softness."
"6245","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Karim al-Aruzzi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Yazid ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray the Fajr prayer at isfar, for it is greater in reward, or: greater for your reward. And this hadith has been disputed concerning Zayd ibn Aslam: Shu'bah narrated it from Abu Dawud, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Rafi' ibn Khadij, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and we do not know Shu'bah narrated with an isnad from Abu Dawud except this hadith, and he is Abu Dawud al-Jazari. And Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Jad, from his grandmother Hawwa', from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and we do not know anyone narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Sa'd except al-Hunayniyy Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, and he was not followed in it."
"6246","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, saying: Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd, from his father, from Anas who informed him, saying: We arrived with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a companion of ours entered to relieve himself, so he took a brick to clean himself with, and it scattered gold dust upon him; he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so he said: Weigh it; and it was two hundred dirhams. He said: This is buried treasure, and in it is the fifth. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Anas except through this channel; and we do not know Zayd ibn Aslam narrated with an isnad from Anas except three hadiths: these two hadiths, and a hadith narrated by Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz from Zayd ibn Aslam from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for Hajj and 'Umrah."
"6247","Al-Hasan ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Jarawi and Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us, saying: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Anas."
"6248","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Ja'far ibn 'Awn narrated to us, Salamah ibn Wardan informed us, from Anas who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said to him: Have you married? He said: I have nothing with which to marry. He said: Is not 'Say: He is Allah, the One' with you? He said: Yes. He said: A quarter of the Qur'an. He said: Is not 'When the help of Allah and the victory come' with you? He said: Yes. He said: A quarter of the Qur'an. He said: Is not 'Say: O you disbelievers' with you? He said: Yes. He said: A quarter of the Qur'an. He said: Is not 'Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer' with you? He said: Yes. He said: A quarter of the Qur'an. He said: Marry, marry. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Anas, nor from other than Anas, with this wording."
"6249","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Wardan who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Say: O you disbelievers' equals a quarter of the Qur'an."
"6250","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Ja'far ibn 'Awn narrated to us, Salamah ibn Wardan informed us, saying: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Which supplication is best? He said: Ask your Lord for pardon and well-being. Then he came to him on the second day and said: Which supplication is best? He said: Ask your Lord for pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter. Then he came to him on the third day and said: Which supplication is best? He said: Ask your Lord for pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter, for if you are given pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter, you have succeeded."
"6251","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Ja'far ibn 'Awn informed us, Salamah ibn Wardan informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to relieve himself and none followed him except 'Umar; he followed him with an earthen vessel of water. He found him prostrating, so he withdrew from him until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head, then he said: You did well, O 'Umar, when you withdrew from me. Jibril came to me and said: Whoever sends one blessing upon you, Allah sends ten blessings upon him, and there is raised for him, I think he said: ten degrees."
"6252","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Ja'far ibn 'Awn narrated to us, Salamah ibn Wardan informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who among you is fasting today? So 'Umar said: I am. Then he said: Who has visited a sick person? So 'Umar said: I have. He said: Who has attended a funeral? So 'Umar said: I have. Then he said: It has become binding, it has become binding."
"6253","And with his isnad he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended one step of the minbar and said: Amin; then he ascended another step and said: Amin; then he ascended the third and said: Amin; then he sat. He said: So they asked him: For what did you say Amin, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Jibril came to me and said: May the nose of a man be rubbed in dust, in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not send blessings upon you. I said: Amin. And may the nose of a man be rubbed in dust who reaches one or both of his parents and does not enter Paradise. I said: Amin. And may the nose of a man be rubbed in dust who reaches Ramadan and is not forgiven. I said: Amin. And we do not know anyone narrated the hadiths of Salamah with these wordings other than he, from Anas, nor from other than Anas. And Salamah is righteous, and his hadiths were narrated by none other than him, as if unfamiliarity is felt from them."
"6254","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu 'Amir al-'Aqadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Seek the hour that is hoped for on Friday between the 'Asr prayer and sunset. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Anas except through this channel; and Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd has narrated hadiths that were not corroborated, though people have tolerated his hadith."
"6255","Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Bahr and Muhammad ibn 'Abbad narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Za'idah who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The place of a whip in Paradise is better than this world and what is in it. And Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Za'idah, we do not know he narrated from Anas except this hadith; and he is a man of Madinah."
"6256","Salih ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Sabiq narrated to us, saying: I read to Muhammad ibn Ishaq: 'Asim ibn 'Umar ibn Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas who said: I saw the cloak of Ukaydir when it was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Muslims began to marvel at it, so he said: Do you marvel at this? By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the handkerchiefs of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh in Paradise are better than this."
"6257","And Yusuf ibn Hammad narrated it to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from 'Asim ibn 'Umar, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"6258","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from 'Asim ibn 'Umar ibn Qatadah, from Anas, who said: We used to pray with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I think he said: 'Asr, then one going would go to such-and-such a place while the sun was still as it was, unchanged."
"6259","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu 'Amir narrated to us, Kharijah ibn 'Abd Allah al-Ansari, of the descendants of Zayd ibn Thabit, narrated to us, from his father who said: We returned from Zuhr to Anas ibn Malik with Kharijah ibn Zayd, and he said to the slave-girl: See whether the prayer time has come."
"6260","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman al-'Uqayli, al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah and Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was thrown from a horse and his right side was scraped; they came to him visiting him, so he led them in prayer sitting while they stood, and he signalled to them to sit, so they sat. When he finished his prayer he said: The imam is only appointed to be followed: when he says takbir, say takbir; when he bows, bow; when he says: Allah hears him who praises Him, say: Our Lord, and to You is praise; when he prostrates, prostrate; when he prays standing, pray standing; and when he prays sitting, pray sitting altogether."
"6261","And Muqaddam ibn Muhammad narrated it to us, my uncle Yahya ibn 'Ali ibn Muqaddam narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar narrated to us."
"6262","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us."
"6263","And Ahmad ibn Aban and Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated it to us, saying: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us."
"6264","And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me."
"6265","And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, Ibn al-Had and Yunus narrated to me."
"6266","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us. All of these mentioned from al-Zuhri from Anas something similar to the hadith of Ayyub from al-Zuhri from Anas. Al-Layth said in his hadith from Ibn Shihab: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell from a horse. And Ma'mar said: The Messenger of Allah rode a horse and was thrown. And all of them mentioned something similar to the hadith of Ayyub from al-Zuhri from Anas. And we do not know it narrated from Ayyub except by al-Tufawi, nor from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar except by Ibn Muqaddam and 'Adiyy ibn al-Fadl."
"6267","Ahmad ibn Aban and Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: The last look I cast at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the day he died; I looked at his face as if it were a leaf of a mushaf. He uncovered the curtain and gestured to the people, while the people were in rows behind Abu Bakr; he gestured to them to remain, and let down the hanging curtain, then he died at the end of that day (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6268","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, 'Uqayl narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab who said: Anas ibn Malik informed me that the Muslims, while they were in the Fajr prayer on Monday with Abu Bakr leading them, were suddenly surprised by nothing but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having uncovered the curtain of 'A'ishah's room; he looked at them while they were in the rows of prayer, then he smiled and laughed. They thought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to come out, so they almost became distracted in their prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured with his hand to complete your prayer, then he entered the room and let down the curtain between him and them. That was the last I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on that day."
"6269","And Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated it to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: When it was Monday, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uncovered the curtain of the room while Abu Bakr was leading the people in prayer. I looked at his face as if it were a leaf of a mushaf, while he was smiling. We almost became distracted in our prayer out of joy at seeing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Bakr wanted to step back, so he gestured to him to stay as you are, then he let down the curtain until he passed away on that very day."
"6270","And Bishr ibn Khalid al-'Askari and 'Ubayd ibn Bakhit narrated it to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"6271","Ahmad ibn Aban and Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, who heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered our house, so we milked for him a domestic sheep and mixed it with water from the well of the house. Abu Bakr was on his left, a bedouin on his right, and 'Umar at a side. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank, so 'Umar said: Hand it to Abu Bakr. But he handed it to the bedouin and said: The rightmost, then the rightmost."
"6272","And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank milk, with Abu Bakr on his left and a bedouin on his right; he handed the remainder to the bedouin and said: The rightmost, then the rightmost."
"6273","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Bishr ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6274","And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar to the hadith of Ibn 'Uyaynah."
"6275","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj, Malik ibn Anas, Zakariyya ibn Ishaq, Salih ibn Abi al-Khadir and Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"6276","Ahmad ibn 'Abdah and Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who heard Anas ibn Malik saying, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When supper is present and the prayer is established, begin with supper."
"6277","And 'Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated it to us, Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6278","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, 'Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated to me, from Abu Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet said: When supper is brought near, begin with supper before you pray the Maghrib prayer. I think he said: And do not hasten away from your supper."
"6279","And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When supper is brought near, begin with supper before the Maghrib prayer."
"6280","And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to me, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed us, that Ibn Shihab informed him, saying: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When supper is brought near and the prayer comes, begin with it before you pray the Maghrib prayer."
"6281","Muhammad ibn 'Abdah and Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not turn your backs on one another, do not hate one another, do not envy one another; be servants of Allah as brothers. And it is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."
"6282","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"6283","And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, Yunus narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar to the hadith of Ibn 'Uyaynah."
"6284","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Khalid, meaning Ibn Musafir, narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, that he heard Anas ibn Malik, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."
"6285","Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Hour, so he said: What have you prepared for it? He mentioned that he had not prepared much deed for it except that he says: I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: You will be with whom you love."
"6286","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us, 'Ali ibn Sa'id ibn Shaddad narrated to us, Abu al-Malih al-Hasan ibn 'Umar narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was met by a bedouin who said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: I have not prepared much good for it, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: Then you will be with whom you love."
"6287","Ahmad ibn 'Abdah and Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, saying: Ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade making nabidh in dubba' and muzaffat vessels."
"6288","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6289","And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas."
"6290","And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih and 'Abd ibn Yusuf narrated to us, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab."
"6291","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, Ibn al-Had narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas, from the Prophet who said: Do not make nabidh in dubba' and muzaffat vessels."
"6292","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered on the day of the conquest of Makkah with a helmet upon his head. He was told: Ibn Khatal is clinging to the coverings of the Ka'bah. He said: Kill him."
"6293","And 'Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated it to us, Ibrahim ibn Yahya ibn Hani' narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered in the year of the conquest with a helmet upon his head. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri except Malik and the nephew of al-Zuhri; and we do not know anyone narrated it from the nephew of al-Zuhri except Yahya ibn Hani'."
"6294","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Bishr ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas who said: We used to pray 'Asr, then one going would go to Quba' while the sun was still high."
"6295","And 'Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated it to us, Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we would leave while the sun was still high; one going would go to al-'Awali while the sun was likewise. And this hadith has been narrated by Yunus, Ibn Abi Dhi'b and others from al-Zuhri from Anas."
"6296","Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held a wedding feast for Safiyyah with dates and sawiq. And this hadith, Ibn 'Uyaynah did not hear it from al-Zuhri; he only heard it from Wa'il ibn Dawud, from his son Bakr ibn Wa'il, from al-Zuhri from Anas. And other than Ibn Aban said: From Ibn 'Uyaynah, from Wa'il, from his father, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held a wedding feast for Safiyyah with dates and sawiq."
"6297","Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us, and I found in my book from Ahmad ibn Aban, from Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah when I was ten years old, and he died when I was twenty years old; and my mothers used to urge me to honour him."
"6298","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, 'Uqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik, that he was ten years old when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived. He said: My mothers used to keep me constant in serving the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah for ten years, and he died when I was twenty years old."
"6299","Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Abu Ayyub Sulayman ibn Shurahbil narrated to us, from Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid, from Malik ibn Anas, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best worship is awaiting relief from Allah. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Malik except with the narration of Baqiyyah from him; perhaps Baqiyyah was narrated to by an untrustworthy man from Malik, so he dropped the man and narrated it from Malik, and he did not say: Malik narrated to us. And the hadith is not known except from other than Malik, from al-Zuhri from Anas."
"6300","Salamah ibn Shabib and Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas."
"6301","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali was the most similar of them in face to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri except Ma'mar."
"6302","Salamah ibn Shabib and Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to keep his voice low in prayer. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri from Anas except Ma'mar."
"6303","Salamah ibn Shabib, al-Husayn ibn Mahdi, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad and Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn 'Askar narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah in the 'Umrah of al-Qada', with 'Abd Allah ibn Rawahah holding his stirrup, chanting rajaz. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri from Anas except Ma'mar, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Ma'mar except 'Abd al-Razzaq."
"6304","Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi, Salamah ibn Shabib and Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, the wording being Zuhayr's, saying: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri: Anas ibn Malik informed me that some people of the Ansar on the day of Hunayn said, when Allah the Almighty bestowed upon His Messenger the wealth of Hawazin, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began giving men of Quraysh a hundred camels each, they said: May Allah forgive the Messenger of Allah; he gives Quraysh and leaves us while our swords drip with their blood. Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told of their words, so he sent for the Ansar and gathered them in a tent of leather, with none other than them invited with them. When they gathered, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them and said: What is this report that reached me about you? The Ansar said: As for our men of judgment, they said nothing; as for people young in age, they said such-and-such, for this statement. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I give men to reconcile their hearts, while you return with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to your dwellings. By Allah, what you return with is better than what they return with. They said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will find, or you will see, after me severe favouritism, so be patient until you meet Allah and His Messenger, for I am your predecessor at the Hawd. Anas said: But we did not remain patient."
"6305","And 'Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated it to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shu'ayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from the Prophet, with something similar. And this hadith has been narrated from al-Zuhri from Anas by a group; we have sufficed with those of them we named."
"6306","Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: Fifty prayers were obligated upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then they were reduced until made five; then it was called out: O Muhammad, the word is not changed with Me, and for you with these five is the reward of fifty."
"6307","Zuhayr ibn Muhammad and al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out when the sun had declined, and prayed Zuhr."
"6308","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cauterized As'ad ibn Zurarah on his basilic vein. And this hadith, Ma'mar erred in it as became clear to the scholars of hadith at Basrah, for al-Zuhri narrates it from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl; but thus Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated it from him."
"6309","Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Ahwazi narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from 'Uqayl that he heard Ibn Shihab reporting, from Anas ibn Malik."
"6310","Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated it to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas; the wording is the wording of 'Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day to his companions: A man of the people of Paradise will enter from here. Ma'mar said in his hadith: His beard dripping water from ablution he performed, his sandals hung. Then Sa'd entered. He said that twice, and each time Sa'd came. When 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr heard that, he went with him that night, saying: O uncle, there was some exchange between me and 'Amr, so I wished to spend the night with you. He said: Yes, O son of my brother. So 'Abd Allah spent the night with him, while Sa'd slept; when he stirred in the night he remembered Allah. When morning came he stood, performed ablution, bowed two units, then went out to prayer. He did that for three nights, adding nothing to that. When morning came on the third day, 'Abd Allah said to him: By Allah, there was nothing between me and 'Amr except good; but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying of you: A man of the people of Paradise will enter, so I wished to know what your deed is. Sa'd said to him: It is only what you saw, O son of my brother, except that I do not spend the night bearing malice against any Muslim, or a word to that effect."
"6311","'Ubayd Allah ibn al-Jahm al-Anmati narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Suwayd al-Ramli narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, 'Umar and 'Uthman used to recite: Master of the Day of Judgment. And this hadith, Yunus and 'Uqayl both narrated it from al-Zuhri from Anas; and Ma'mar narrated it from al-Zuhri as mursal."
"6312","Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Waddah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Yunus, meaning Ibn Yazid, narrating from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, place in it twice the blessing You placed in Makkah, meaning Madinah. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri from Anas except Yunus; and Ibn Wahb and others narrated it from Yunus."
"6313","Al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of silver whose stone was Abyssinian, and placed its stone toward the inside of his palm."
"6314","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of silver whose stone was Abyssinian, and engraved upon it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah."
"6315","And Muhammad ibn 'Uqbah narrated it to us, 'Umar ibn Harun al-Balkhi narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And this hadith, only Yunus mentioned its stone being Abyssinian; we do not know anyone who said its stone was Abyssinian except him."
"6316","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, the wording being Nasr's, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us, Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, 'Umar and 'Uthman used to walk in front of the funeral bier. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri from Anas except Muhammad ibn Bakr from Yunus; we do not know anyone followed him in it, and Ibn 'Uyaynah and Ibn Jurayj only narrate it from al-Zuhri from Salim from his father."
"6317","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Ruwaym al-Muqri' narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us from 'Uqayl ibn Khalid, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the land is fertile, give, I think he said: the mounts, their share of pasture; and when the land is barren, pass over it with its marrow, and upon you is travelling by night, for the land is folded at night. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Layth from 'Uqayl from al-Zuhri from Anas except Ruwaym, and he was trustworthy; and others narrated it from al-Zuhri as mursal."
"6318","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us from 'Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves that his provision be expanded for him and his trace be lengthened, let him join his kinship. And this hadith, 'Uqayl narrated it, and Yunus also narrated it from al-Zuhri from Anas."
"6319","Muhammad ibn Isma'il, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad and 'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbuwayh al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore a ring on his right hand. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri from Anas except Yunus, nor from Yunus except Sulayman ibn Bilal."
"6320","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i and Muhammad ibn 'Uthman al-'Uqayli narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding what is made in pitched vessels and in dubba', and every intoxicant is unlawful."
"6321","And Salamah ibn Shabib narrated it to us, Hafs ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is unlawful. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri from Anas except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; it is only narrated from al-Zuhri from Anas concerning dubba' and muzaffat, and Ibn Ishaq added: Every intoxicant is unlawful."
"6322","And 'Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, Ziyad ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever sleeps through a prayer, let him pray it when he remembers it. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from al-Zuhri from Anas except through the narration of Muhammad ibn Ishaq from him; we do not know anyone narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq except Ziyad, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Ziyad except 'Umar ibn Yahya."
"6323","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrating from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: When it was Monday, the day in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, and the door was opened, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out until he stood at the door of 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her. The Muslims almost became distracted by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) out of joy, and they dispersed; he gestured to them to remain firm in your prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled out of delight at what he saw of their state in prayer. I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a finer state than at that hour. Then he returned, and the people left thinking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had recovered from his illness; Abu Bakr returned to his family."
"6324","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, Ahwas ibn Jawwab narrated to us, 'Ammar ibn Zurayq narrated to us from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abi Layla, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his voice with the talbiyah for 'Umrah and Hajj together. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri from Anas except Isma'il ibn Umayyah."
"6325","Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of gold; the people took rings, so one day he threw it away, and the people threw away their rings; then he never wore it again."
"6326","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Abu 'Asim and Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ziyad ibn Sa'd, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that he saw in the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a ring of silver for one day; then the people made rings and wore them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw away his ring, and the people threw away their rings."
"6327","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, 'Uqayl narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas."
"6328","And Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated it to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: If the son of Adam had a valley of gold, he would love to have another valley; nothing fills his mouth but dust, and Allah turns to whoever turns."
"6329","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from 'Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab who said: Anas ibn Malik informed me, saying: I am the most knowledgeable of people concerning the hijab when it was revealed. The first of what was revealed concerning the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was when he consummated marriage with Zaynab bint Jahsh: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awoke as a bridegroom, invited the people, they partook of food, then they left, while a group of them remained with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and prolonged their stay. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and went out, and I went out with him, but they did not leave. He walked until he came to the room of 'A'ishah, thinking they had left; he returned and I returned with him, and there they were, they had left. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck a curtain between me and him, and the hijab was revealed."
"6330","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Bishr ibn 'Umar narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from 'Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wished to combine two prayers, meaning in travel, would delay Zuhr until the time of 'Asr entered, then combine them; and when he wished to combine Maghrib and 'Isha', he would delay Maghrib until the time of 'Isha' entered, then combine them."
"6331","Muhammad ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Yazid ibn Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Mawhab narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from 'Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he set out before the sun declined, would delay Zuhr until the time of 'Asr, then alight and combine them; if the sun declined before he set out, he would pray Zuhr, then mount."
"6332","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib and 'Uqayl ibn Khalid, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man selling the stud service of his stallion."
"6333","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib and 'Uqayl narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Mariyah his slave-girl, was born, something entered the heart of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about him, until Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and said: Peace be upon you, O father of Ibrahim. And these hadiths, we do not know anyone narrated them from al-Zuhri from Anas except 'Uqayl."
"6334","Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from 'Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Bilal to make the adhan even-numbered and the iqamah odd-numbered. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the hadith of al-Zuhri from Anas except through this channel."
"6335","Muhammad ibn Miskin, 'Umar ibn al-Khattab and Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn 'Askar narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi' ibn Yazid narrated to us, from 'Uqayl ibn Khalid, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Prophet of Allah Ayyub, peace be upon him, remained in his affliction for eighteen years; near and far abandoned him except two men of his brothers who were among his closest brothers, who would come to him morning and evening. One of them said to his companion: Do you know, by Allah, he has certainly committed a sin no one in the worlds has committed? His companion said to him: And what is that? He said: He has been afflicted for eighteen years, and Allah has not had mercy on him to remove what is with him. When he saw his condition, the man could not remain patient until he mentioned that to him. So Ayyub said: I do not know what you say, except that Allah knows of me that I used to pass by two men disputing while they mentioned Allah the Blessed and Exalted, so I would return to my house and make expiation for them, lest they mention Allah except in truth. He would go out to relieve himself, and when he finished, his wife would hold his hand until he reached. When one day she was late for him, it was revealed to Ayyub in his place: Strike with your foot; this is a cool bath and drink. He said: She found him late, so she met him looking; he came toward her with Allah having removed his affliction, in the finest state he had been. When she saw him she said: O may Allah bless you, have you seen this afflicted Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? By Allah, I have never seen anyone more like him when healthy than you. He said: Then I am he. He said: He had two threshing-floors: a threshing-floor for wheat and a threshing-floor for barley. Allah the Blessed and Exalted sent two clouds; when one was over the wheat threshing-floor it poured gold into it until it overflowed, and the other poured silver into the barley threshing-floor until it overflowed. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri from Anas except 'Uqayl, and none narrated it from 'Uqayl except Nafi' ibn Yazid; and more than one narrated it from Nafi'."
"6336","Al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to me, Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank milk while standing, with a bedouin on his right and Abu Bakr on his left; he gave the bedouin his remainder and said: The rightmost, then the rightmost."
"6337","And Ibn Miskin narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank milk while standing."
"6338","Muhammad ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, Suwayd ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us, Qurrah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent when he was forty years old; he remained in Makkah ten years, and in Madinah ten years, and he died when he was sixty, with not twenty white hairs in his head and beard."
"6339","Muhammad ibn Rizq Allah al-Kalwadhani narrated to us, Bishr ibn Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In my Hawd there are jugs as many as the stars of the sky."
"6340","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl and Ibrahim ibn Ziyad narrated to us, saying: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Allah the Blessed and Exalted sent revelation in succession upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the most abundant revelation was on the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died."
"6341","Muhammad ibn 'Isa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Uzayz narrated to us, Salamah ibn Rawh narrated to us, from 'Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Most of the people of Paradise are the simple-minded; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Many a weak and downtrodden one, if he swore by Allah, He would fulfill it. And this hadith, part of its wording has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through various channels, and part of it we do not know narrated except through this channel. And Salamah was the nephew of 'Uqayl ibn Khalid; he was not followed in the hadith: Most of the people of Paradise are the simple-minded, though were it sound it would have a meaning."
"6342","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to us, from his brother Abu 'Ali ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it: And the eye for the eye. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri from Anas except Abu 'Ali ibn Yazid, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Yunus except Ibn al-Mubarak."
"6343","'Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Malik Abu Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Qatadah al-'Udhri narrated to us, the nephew of al-Zuhri narrated to us, from his uncle, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Even if the believer were in a burrow, one who harms him, or he said: a hypocrite who harms him, would be sent to him therein."
"6344","And with his isnad: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant lives to forty years in Islam but Allah averts from him kinds of affliction: madness, leprosy and vitiligo. When he reaches fifty years, Allah eases his reckoning for him. When he reaches sixty years, Allah grants him return to Him with what He loves. When he reaches seventy, Allah loves him and the people of heaven love him. When he reaches eighty, Allah accepts his good deeds and overlooks his evil deeds. When he reaches ninety, Allah forgives his past and future sins, he is called Allah's captive on His earth, and intercession is granted for him for his household. And these two hadiths, we do not know anyone narrated them except Abu Qatadah from the nephew of al-Zuhri."
"6345","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas."
"6346","And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us, Sa'id ibn Kathir narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"6347","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, saying: Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar."
"6348","And al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Uhud, he heard the women of the Ansar weeping, so he said: But Hamzah has no weeping women for him. That reached the women of the Ansar, so they wept for Hamzah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept and awoke while they were weeping, so he said: Woe to them! Have they continued weeping since today? Let them be silent, and let them not weep for any dead after today."
"6349","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon Hamzah on the day of Uhud and stood over him, seeing he had been mutilated. He said: Were it not that Safiyyah would feel it in herself, I would have left him until the beasts ate him in their bellies. Then he called for a striped cloak and shrouded him in it; when it was drawn over his legs his head was uncovered, and when drawn over his head his legs showed. He said: The slain were many and garments were few. He said: Two and three men were shrouded in a single garment, then buried in one grave. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would ask about them: Which of them knew most Qur'an? Then he would place him toward the qiblah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) buried them and did not pray over them. And this hadith, we do not know anyone followed Usamah in its narration from al-Zuhri from Anas; al-Zuhri narrated it from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik from Jabir."
"6350","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj who said: I know it only from al-Zuhri from Anas."
"6351","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, al-Hajjaj and Sa'id ibn 'Amir narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made a ring; when he entered the privy he removed his ring. Ibn Ma'mar had no doubt in his narration from Hajjaj nor from Sa'id ibn 'Amir; Hudbah said: When he entered the privy he laid down his ring, adding nothing to that."
"6352","Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn a dead person for more than three days, except for a husband. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri from Anas except Zam'ah."
"6353","Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Abu 'Asim narrated to us, Zam'ah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank milk and rinsed his mouth, saying: It has fat. And this hadith, the muhaddithun only narrate it from al-Zuhri from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Utbah from Ibn 'Abbas; I think Zam'ah erred in his hadith."
"6354","Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam and Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, the wording being Muhammad's, saying: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas."
"6355","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah while it was feverish; he entered the mosque while the people were praying sitting, so he said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing. So the people exerted themselves to pray standing. The wording is the wording of Muhammad ibn Bakr. And this hadith has been disputed concerning al-Zuhri: 'Abd al-Razzaq and Muhammad ibn Bakr said: From Ibn Jurayj from al-Zuhri from Anas; Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar followed them in their narration."
"6356","Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Idris narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: I saw us trading in slave-mothers while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us."
"6357","'Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbuwayh al-Marwazi and 'Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, saying: 'Utbah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the sick person when he recovers and is cured of his illness is like a hailstone falling from the sky in its purity and colour. And al-Walid ibn Muhammad is soft in hadith; called al-Muwaqqari; he narrated from al-Zuhri hadiths in some of which he was not followed."
"6358","Harun ibn Abi 'Alqamah al-Farawi wrote to me, informing that Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to him from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas."
"6359","And Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated it to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Uqbah narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas."
"6360","And Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated it to us, Abu 'Amr, I think Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Ansar sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, permit us to forgo the ransom of our nephew al-'Abbas. He said: No, not even a dirham."
"6361","Harun ibn Abi 'Alqamah al-Farawi wrote to me, informing that Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to him from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that some people of 'Uraynah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he sent them among his camels, but they killed the shepherd and drove off the camels, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off their hands and legs. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri from Anas except Musa ibn 'Uqbah."
"6362","Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu 'Amr al-Lakhmi, meaning Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: There was a slave-girl of 'Abd Allah ibn Ubayy called Mu'adhah whom he forced into adultery; when Islam came, there was revealed: And do not force your slave-girls into prostitution, up to His saying: Then Allah, after their compulsion, is Forgiving, Merciful. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from al-Zuhri from Anas except through this channel."
"6363","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd al-Ghaffar ibn 'Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: I used to pour the ablution water of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for all his wives, or he said: water for his bath for all his wives. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except through this channel."
"6364","One of our companions narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn Musa, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that a man was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); a son of his came, so he kissed him and seated him upon his thigh, while a little daughter of his came and he seated her before him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not treat them equally? And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Ma'mar except 'Abd Allah ibn Musa, and he was a San'ani who moved to Makkah."
"6365","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, 'Ubadah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri who said: I entered upon Anas ibn Malik in his tent during the caliphate of 'Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan while he was distressed. I said: I hope Allah has not kept you back except to be a witness against this ummah. He said: They have come to morning and evening contradicting those before them, except that they pray, and in prayer there is delay. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from al-Zuhri from Anas except through this channel."
"6366","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ibn Shihab informed me, from Anas who said: The last look I cast at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was that he fell ill, so he commanded Abu Bakr, who led the people in prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uncovered the curtain of 'A'ishah's room while the people were looking; I looked at his face as if it were a leaf of a mushaf, until Abu Bakr stepped back upon his heels, thinking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wished to lead the people in prayer. He gestured to them to complete their prayer, and let down the curtain between them and him; he died on that very day (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6367","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ibn Shihab informed me, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell from a horse and his right side was scraped, so he led them in prayer sitting. When he finished he said: The imam is only appointed to be followed: when he prays standing, pray standing; when he bows, bow; when he rises, rise; when he prostrates, prostrate; when he says: Allah hears him who praises Him, say: Our Lord, and to You is praise; and when he prays sitting, pray sitting altogether."
"6368","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Jabr, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe with five makakiyy and perform ablution with a makkuk. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Anas, nor from other than Anas, with this wording except through this channel."
"6369","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Jabr, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe with some of his wives from a single vessel."
"6370","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Jabr, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sign of the hypocrite is hatred of the Ansar, and the sign of faith is love of the Ansar."
"6371","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Mawhab, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, saying: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatimah: What prevents you from hearing what I counsel you with, to say morning and evening: O Living, O Sustainer, by Your mercy I seek aid; set right all my affair for me, and do not leave me to myself for the blink of an eye. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Anas except through this channel with this isnad."
"6372","Harun ibn Sufyan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ya'la al-Muharibi narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn 'Ujrah, from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a drink, with Abu Bakr on his left, a bedouin on his right, and 'Umar facing him. He drank, and 'Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, this is Abu Bakr, showing him his place. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those on the right, and he gave the bedouin."
"6373","Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, meaning Ibn 'Ulayyah, narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to perfume himself with saffron."
"6374","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abbad al-Huna'i narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade saffron perfume. Abu Bakr said: He only forbade a man perfuming himself with saffron, but Shu'bah erred in it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it except Isma'il ibn Ibrahim."
"6375","'Abd Allah ibn Abi Ya'qub al-Kirmani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas who said: The most frequent supplication the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated with was: O Allah, give us in this world good, and in the Hereafter good, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire."
"6376","And Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated it to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Suhayb who said: Qatadah asked Anas: Which supplication did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) most often supplicate with? He said: The most frequent supplication he supplicated with was: O Allah, give us in this world good, and in the Hereafter good, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. And we do not know Shu'bah narrated with an isnad from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim except these two hadiths."
"6377","Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided Khaybar; we prayed near it the dawn prayer in darkness. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mounted, Abu Talhah mounted, and Abu Talhah took me behind him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proceeded in the alley of Khaybar until his thigh was uncovered, so that I was looking at the whiteness of the thigh of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he entered the town he said: Allah is Greatest; when we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned, saying it three times. The people came out to their works, saying: Muhammad and the khamis; and the khamis is the army. We seized it, the captives were gathered, and Dihyah came saying: O Prophet of Allah, grant me a slave-girl from the captives. He said: Go and take a slave-girl. He went and took Safiyyah bint Huyayy. A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Messenger of Allah, you gave Dihyah Safiyyah bint Huyayy, the mistress of Qurayzah and al-Nadir; she befits none but you. He said: Call him with her. He brought her; when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at her he said: Take a slave-girl from the captives other than her. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed her and married her. I said: O Abu Hamzah, what did he give her as dowry? He said: Herself; he freed her and married her. When on the road, Umm Sulaym prepared her for him at night; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awoke as a bridegroom, saying: Whoever has anything, let him bring it to me. He spread a leather mat; a man would bring dried yoghurt, a man would bring dates, a man would bring ghee, a man would bring sawiq, until they made hays. That was the wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6378","Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you wish for death because of harm that befalls him; if he must wish, let him say: O Allah, keep me alive while life is good for me, and take me when death is good for me."
"6379","Mu'ammal narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you supplicates, let him be resolute in supplication, and let him not say: O Allah, if You will, give me; for Allah the Blessed and Exalted has none who compels Him."
"6380","Mu'ammal narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to delay the prayer and complete it."
"6381","Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us; Isma'il narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a ring made and said: I have had a ring made and engraved an engraving upon it, so let no one engrave upon it."
"6382","And with the same chain; he said: The prayer was established and a man intercepted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for some need, and he did not rise for the prayer until the people had dozed off."
"6383","And with the same chain; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice two rams. Anas said: And I sacrifice two rams."
"6384","And with the same chain; he said: A funeral passed by and it was praised with good, so the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has become due, it has become due, it has become due. And a funeral passed by and it was spoken of with evil, so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has become due, it has become due, it has become due. Umar said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, a funeral passed by and it was praised with good and you said: It has become due, and a funeral passed by and it was spoken of with evil and you said: It has become due? He said: Whomever you praise with good, Paradise has become due for him, and whomever you speak of with evil, the Fire has become due for him. For you are the witnesses of Allah upon the earth."
"6385","And with the same chain; he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the lavatory he said: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the male and female devils."
"6386","And with the same chain; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."
"6387","And with the same chain; he said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal used to lead his people in prayer, then Haram came in wanting to water his date-palms, so he entered the mosque to pray with the people. When he saw Mu'adh - I think he said - prolonging, he shortened his prayer and joined his date-palms to water them. When Mu'adh finished the prayer, or completed the prayer, it was said to him: So-and-so entered the mosque, and when he saw you prolonging he shortened his prayer and joined his date-palms to water them. So Haram came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while Mu'adh was with him, and said: O Prophet of Allah, I wanted to water my date-palms, so I entered the mosque to pray with the people, and when he prolonged I shortened my prayer and joined my date-palms to water them, yet he claims I am a hypocrite. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to Mu'adh and said: Are you a maker of trial, are you a maker of trial? Do not prolong for them; recite: Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High, and: By the sun and its brightness, and the like. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb except Isma'il ibn Ibrahim."
"6388","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Umarah, in whom there is no harm, narrated to us; Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things will not cease in my nation until the Hour comes: wailing, boasting of lineages, and seeking rain by the stars."
"6389","And with the same chain; he said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for ten years, and he never said to me for anything I did: Why did you do it, nor for anything I did not do: Why did you not do it, or the like of that. And I never touched silk softer than the palm of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6390","And with the same chain; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has three children die before reaching maturity, Allah will admit him to Paradise by virtue of His mercy toward them."
"6391","And with the same chain; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to perfume his skin with saffron."
"6392","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Mada'ini narrated to us; Warqa' ibn Umar narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to breathe in the vessel three times. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abd al-Aziz except Warqa'."
"6393","Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Rasi, who was from the people of Ra's al-Ayn, narrated to us; Mu'ammal narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man supplicates for his brother in his absence, the angels say: Amen, and for you the like. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Hammad ibn Salamah except Mu'ammal."
"6394","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mufaddal al-Harrani narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah al-Mada'ini narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prophets are alive, praying in their graves. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who corroborated al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah in his narration from Hammad; rather it is narrated from Anas through the hadith of Thabit and others, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw Musa (peace be upon him) praying in his grave."
"6395","Muhammad ibn Mirdas al-Ansari narrated to us; Mubarak Abu Suhaym, the freedman of Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: One killed defending his property is a martyr."
"6396","And with the same chain; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No two Muslims meet with their swords but that the killer and the killed are in the Fire."
"6397","And with the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Hasten with deeds before six: the rising of the sun from its setting, the Dajjal, the smoke, the beast, the private affair of one of you, and the general affair."
"6398","And with the same chain; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Time will only increase in severity, people will only increase in stinginess, and the Hour will only come upon the worst of people."
"6399","And with the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to his companions: The world is sweet and green; and Allah has made you stewards over it and sees how you act, so beware of the world and beware of women."
"6400","And with the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There will be in my nation sinking, transformation, and pelting."
"6401","And with the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Seventy thousand of my nation will enter Paradise without reckoning: they are those who do not seek cauterization, nor practice cauterization, nor seek incantations, nor take omens, and upon their Lord they rely."
"6402","And with the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to his companions: Let me not find you returning after me as disbelievers, striking the necks of one another. And Mubarak, the freedman of Abd al-Aziz, narrated many hadiths from Abd al-Aziz, among them objectionable hadiths for which he was not corroborated, so these hadiths were taken from his hadiths because they were not known from Anas, while most of them are known from other than Anas. And I do not know that Mubarak narrated from anyone other than Abd al-Aziz."
"6403","Muhammad ibn Bashar narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - I think he said - used to command lightening the prayer."
"6404","And with the same chain; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."
"6405","And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qut'i narrated it to us; Abd al-A'la narrated to us; Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"6406","And with the same chain; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wears silk in the world will not wear it in the Hereafter."
"6407","And with the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he sacrificed two rams. Anas said: And I sacrifice two rams."
"6408","And with the same chain: that a funeral passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they praised it with good, so he said: It has become due. And a funeral passed by and they spoke of it with evil, so he said: It has become due. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, you said for the first: It has become due, and you said for the other: It has become due? He said: As for the first, Paradise has become due for him, and as for the other, the Fire has become due for him. You are the witnesses of Allah upon the earth."
"6409","And with the same chain; he said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) give a wedding feast for any of his wives greater than what he gave for Zaynab, for he fed them bread and meat until they were satiated."
"6410","And with the same chain; he said: The prayer was established - I think he said - then a man stood speaking to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until his companions, or some of his companions, slept. Then he rose and prayed."
"6411","And with the same chain; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Safiyyah and gave her a dowry. I said: What did he give her as dowry? He said: Herself; and he married her."
"6412","And with the same chain; he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the lavatory he said: I seek refuge in Allah from the male and female devils."
"6413","Muhammad ibn Miskin and Harun ibn Sufyan narrated to us; they said: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had abundant curly hair. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shu'bah except Muhammad ibn al-Qasim. Muhammad ibn al-Qasim narrated hadiths for which he was not corroborated, though Ibn al-Mubarak narrated from him."
"6414","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us; Shabab narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to shorten it yet complete it, meaning the prayer."
"6415","Muhammad ibn Bashar and Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us; they said: Abu Dawud narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi and Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb and Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman and Attab the freedman of Hurmuz, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"6416","Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated to us; Mubarak, the freedman of Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, narrated to us; Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I am the master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast; I am the first for whom the earth will split open on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast; I am the first to enter Paradise, and no boast; I am the first intercessor and the first whose intercession is accepted. In my hand is the banner of praise on the Day of Resurrection; Adam and those below him are under my banner. Then I come to my Lord, blessed and exalted, and it is said to me: Who? And I say: Ahmad. Then it is opened for me, and when I see my Lord, mighty and majestic, I fall prostrate to Him, and I praise Him with praises that none before me nor after me has praised Him with, which Allah, blessed and exalted, inspires me with. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abd al-Aziz except Mubarak, and we have already mentioned him. Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb is trustworthy; the leading scholars narrated from him."
"6417","Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us; Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us; Shayban - meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman - narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ishaq, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will come until he alights in the vicinity of Madinah, then Madinah will tremble with three tremors, and every hypocrite will go out to him."
"6418","Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Ishaq, from Anas, who said: Umm Sulaym asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to come to her house and pray in it so she could take it as a place of prayer. One day she took a mat of theirs and sprinkled it with water, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and they prayed with him. And this hadith was narrated from Ishaq by a group, among them Ubaydullah ibn Umar, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, Abdullah ibn Umar, Malik ibn Anas, and others. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari except Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi."
"6419","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us; Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us; al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Ishaq, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of the Jews of Isfahan - or of the Jewish quarter of Isfahan - wearing tayalisah will follow the Dajjal."
"6420","And with the same chain; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque one day wearing a thick Najrani cloak with a border, then a bedouin came from behind him and seized the two sides of the garment and pulled it until the border left a mark on the side of the neck of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said to him: Give us from the wealth of Allah which He has given you. He said: So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to him, smiled, and said: Order for him, or: Give him. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Ishaq, from Anas; Malik narrated it."
"6421","Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us; al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Ishaq, from Anas, who said: Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, does a woman who sees in a dream what a man sees have to wash? Umm Salamah said: You have disgraced women, O Umm Sulaym. He said: If she sees that, let her wash. Umm Salamah said: And do women have fluid? He said: Yes; they are but the counterparts of men. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Anas, and we do not know anyone who brought the wording of Ishaq."
"6422","And with the same chain; he said: I never prayed behind anyone whose prayer was lighter yet complete than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6423","And with the same chain; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will tread every town except Makkah and Madinah. As for Madinah, the angels - I think he said - are over it, or prevent him from it, so it trembles with three tremors, and no disbeliever or hypocrite remains but goes out to him."
"6424","Ubaydullah ibn Yusuf al-Thaqafi narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Salm narrated to us; al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Ishaq, from Anas: that Abu Talhah used to shoot before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: My soul for your soul as ransom, and my face as a shield for your face."
"6425","Zayd ibn Akhzam Abu Talib al-Ta'i narrated to us; Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us; Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us; Ishaq narrated to us; Anas narrated to me, saying: Umm Sulaym had an orphan girl with her, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw the orphan girl and said: You have grown old; may your age not advance. The orphan girl returned to Umm Sulaym weeping, so Umm Sulaym said: What is wrong with you, my daughter? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated against me that my age not advance. Umm Sulaym went out until she met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: What is wrong with you, O Umm Sulaym? She said: O Messenger of Allah, you supplicated against my orphan girl that her age not advance. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, then said: O Umm Sulaym, do you not know my condition with my Lord, mighty and majestic? I stipulated with my Lord and said: I am but a human who is pleased as humans are pleased and angered as humans are angered; so whichever of my nation I supplicate against with a supplication he does not deserve, let Him make it for him a purification, a cleansing, and a nearness by which He draws him near on the Day of Resurrection. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ishaq except Ikrimah."
"6426","And with the same chain; he said: Umm Sulaym came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having wrapped me in her head-cover and clothed me with a veil, and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is my son Anas; I have brought him to you to supplicate for him. He said: O Allah, increase his wealth and his children. Anas said: By Allah, my wealth is indeed abundant and my children so-and-so."
"6427","And with the same chain; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought forgiveness for the Ansar, for the offspring of the Ansar, for the offspring of the offspring of the Ansar, and for the freedmen of the Ansar."
"6428","And with the same chain; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant when he repents to Him than one of you who was upon his mount, then it escaped from him with his food and drink upon it, so he despaired of it, then came to a tree and rested in its shade, having despaired of his mount. While he is like that, there it is standing before him, so from his joy he uttered a word: You are my servant and I am your Lord."
"6429","And with the same chain; he said: While we were in the mosque with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a bedouin came and stood urinating in the mosque, so the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rose toward him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not interrupt him. They left him until he urinated, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had him brought and said: These mosques are not fit for any of this urine or filth; they are only for the remembrance of Allah, prayer, and recitation of the Quran. Then he said to a man of the people, and a man came with a bucket of water and poured it over it."
"6430","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us; they said: Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us; Ikrimah narrated to us; Ishaq narrated to me, from Anas: that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, we were in a house in which our number was many and our wealth abundant, then we moved to a house - I think he said - in which our number became few and our wealth little. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave it, for it is blameworthy. And this hadith - we do not know it narrated from Anas except by this route with this chain."
"6431","Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us; Umar narrated to us; Ikrimah narrated to us, from Ishaq, from Anas, who said: And Quran was revealed concerning them, meaning the companions of Bi'r Ma'unah: Convey to our people from us that we have met our Lord and He is pleased with us and has pleased us. Then it was abrogated and lifted, and there was revealed: And do not think those killed in the way of Allah dead; rather alive with their Lord, provided for."
"6432","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us; Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Ikrimah ibn Ammar, from Ishaq, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to interpret by names. Abu Bakr said: Meaning dreams. And this hadith - we do not know it narrated except from Anas, and other than Ishaq narrated it, and we do not know it narrated from Ishaq except by this route."
"6433","Bistam ibn al-Fadl, the brother of Arim, narrated to us; Abu Qutaybah narrated to us; Hammam narrated to us, from Ishaq, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought old dates and began to inspect them. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Anas except Ishaq."
"6434","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qut'i narrated to us; Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us; Hammam narrated to us, from Ishaq, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to come to his family by night."
"6435","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Hibban - meaning Ibn Hilal - narrated to us; Hammam narrated to us, from Ishaq, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not enter upon any woman of the Ansar except Umm Sulaym, saying: I have mercy on her; her brother was killed with me."
"6436","Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Kabir al-Attar, al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Uruzzi, and al-Sakan ibn Sa'id narrated to us; they said: Amr ibn Asim narrated to us; Hammam narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a prescribed punishment, so establish it upon me - and he did not ask him about it - and the prayer came, so he prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he said: O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a prescribed punishment, so establish the Book of Allah concerning me. He said: Did you not witness the prayer with us? He said: Yes. He said: Then Allah has forgiven you. And this hadith - we do not know it narrated from Anas except by this route, nor did anyone narrate it from Ishaq except Hammam, nor from Hammam except Amr ibn Asim."
"6437","Zayd ibn Akhzam and al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us; they said: Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muhaqalah, muzabanah, and mukhadarah. And this hadith - we do not know it narrated from Anas except by this route, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ishaq except Yunus ibn al-Qasim."
"6438","Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ishaq, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: In the name of Allah, I rely upon Allah, there is no power nor strength except through Allah, it is said: You are sufficed, you are protected, you are guided, and Satan withdraws from him. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Jurayj except Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi, and we do not know that Ibn Jurayj narrated from Ishaq except this hadith."
"6439","Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Shaybah narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ya'qub, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Ishaq, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. And we do not know that Abd al-Rahman narrated with a chain from Ishaq, from Anas, except this hadith."
"6440","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Janah narrated to us; Hilal ibn al-Jahm narrated to us; Ishaq narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aslam and Ghifar and men of Muzaynah and Juhaynah are better than the two confederates Ghatfan and Banu Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah. Uyaynah ibn Badr said: By Allah, to be among these in the Fire - meaning Ghatfan and Banu Amir - is more beloved to me than to be with those in Paradise."
"6441","Khallad ibn Aslam al-Marwazi narrated to us; al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ishaq, from Anas, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you not marry among the Ansar? He said: There is jealousy in them. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Hammad except al-Nadr."
"6442","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ishaq, from Anas: that Hawazin came on the day of Hunayn with children, women, camels, and sheep, and arranged them in rows to outnumber the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Muslims met the polytheists, and the Muslims turned fleeing as Allah, exalted, said. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O servants of Allah, I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. Then he said: O company of the Ansar, I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. So Allah defeated the polytheists, without striking with a sword or thrusting with a spear. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that day: Whoever kills a disbeliever, his spoils are his. Abu Talhah killed twenty men that day and took their spoils. Abu Qatadah said: O Messenger of Allah, I struck a man on the shoulder-joint while he wore a coat of mail, but I was hurried away from taking it, so see with whom it is. A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, I took it, so compensate him from it and give it to me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent - and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never asked for anything but he gave it or remained silent - so Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Allah will not bestow it upon a lion of His lions and give it to you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed and said: Umar has spoken the truth. He said: Abu Talhah met Umm Sulaym with a dagger with her, and said: O Umm Sulaym, what is this with you? She said: By Allah, I intended that if any of them came near me I would rip open his belly. Abu Talhah informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of that, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has sufficed and done good. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ishaq, from Anas, except Hammad alone."
"6443","And I heard Sulayman ibn Ubaydullah mention from Abu Dawud: Hammad ibn Salamah and Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ishaq, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And this hadith - we heard it only from Sulayman, and he was truthful. I think Abu Dawud confused the hadith of Hammad ibn Salamah from Shu'bah and erred in it, or Sulayman erred in it; and we found it in his book thus."
"6444","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us; Marwan ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Ishaq, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most cheerful of people with a child. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ishaq except Umarah, nor do we know that Umarah narrated from Ishaq except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it from Umarah except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"6445","Muhammad ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Misri narrated to us; Hani' ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ishaq and Aban, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four are of wretchedness: a tearless eye, a hard heart, long hope, and greed for the world."
"6446","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us; Hani' ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ishaq, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things - whoever has them deserves reward and completes faith: character by which he lives among people, piety which restrains him from the prohibitions of Allah, and forbearance by which he repels the ignorance of the ignorant."
"6447","And with the same chain, he raised it, saying: A caller will call: Leave the world to its people, leave the world to its people, leave the world to its people - three times. Whoever takes from the world more than suffices him takes a carcass without realizing. And these hadiths - we do not know them narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by this route, from Anas. Abdullah ibn Sulayman narrated hadiths for which he was not corroborated, from al-Maqburi and others, and we do not know anyone who narrated these hadiths from him except Hani' ibn al-Mutawakkil. We mentioned them only because we do not retain them from the hadith of anyone else."
"6448","Amr ibn Isa narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ishaq, from Anas, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and an orphan behind him, and our mother behind us."
"6449","Al-Sakan ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us, from Abdullah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Differ from the Magians: trim the mustaches and leave the beards full."
"6450","Yusuf ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Mus'ab ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Abdullah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of gatherings are the most spacious. And this hadith - we do not know it narrated from Anas except by this route with this chain."
"6451","Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Thabit and Isma'il, from Anas: that Abu Talhah came to Umm Sulaym to propose to her before he became Muslim, and she said to him: Would I marry you while you worship a piece of wood carved by my slave so-and-so? If you become Muslim I will marry you. He said: So Abu Talhah became Muslim and married her upon his Islam. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Hammad combining Thabit and Isma'il except Yazid ibn Harun."
"6452","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us; Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Anas, who said: Perfume was never offered to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but he accepted it. And this hadith - we do not know it narrated from Isma'il except through the hadith of Mubarak."
"6453","And I heard Muhammad ibn Abi Ghalib mention from Mahbub ibn Musa Abu Salih al-Farra', from Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak, from al-Mubarak ibn Fadalah, from Ishaq and Isma'il, the two sons of Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas, who said: Perfume was never offered to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but he accepted it. And this hadith - we mentioned it only because we do not know Mubarak narrating from Ishaq ibn Abdullah, nor do we know anyone who combined them except Ibn al-Mubarak from Mubarak ibn Fadalah."
"6454","Al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us; Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Hafs, the nephew of Anas, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Ansar are my inner garment and my store. So he enjoined good toward the Ansar: to accept from their doers of good and overlook their offenders, for they have fulfilled what was upon them and what is for them remains."
"6455","Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah al-Baghdadi ibn Malaj al-Anmati, trustworthy, narrated to us; Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Hafs, from Anas, who said: Some people of the Ansar had a camel upon which they drew water, and it became unruly and denied them its back. The Ansar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we had a camel upon which we drew water, and it has become unruly and denied us its back. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Rise. They rose with him and came to a garden, with the camel in a corner. He walked toward it. They said: O Messenger of Allah, it has become like a dog, and we fear for you from it, or: we fear for you its attack. He said: There is no harm upon me from it. When the camel saw him, it came walking until it fell prostrate before him. His companions said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a beast that does not reason, while we reason; we are more entitled to prostrate to you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing is fit to prostrate to anything; and had anything been fit to prostrate to anything, I would have commanded the woman to prostrate to her husband, because of the greatness of his right over her. And this hadith - we do not know it narrated with this wording from Anas except by this chain; and as for Hafs, the nephew of Anas, we do not know anyone who narrated from him except Khalaf ibn Khalifah."
"6456","Muhammad ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us; Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us; Hafs narrated to us, from Anas: that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when they passed a man standing in prayer. When the man finished the prayer and sat, he testified and supplicated, saying: O Allah, I ask You by that all praise is Yours, there is no god but You, the Bestower, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know with what he supplicated? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: He supplicated with His greatest name, by which if He is called upon He answers, and if asked by it He gives."
"6457","And with the same chain; he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came and said: Peace upon you and the mercy of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: And upon you, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. When the man sat he said: Praise be to Allah, abundant, good, blessed praise, as our Lord loves to be praised. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How did you say? He repeated as he had said, and he said: By Him in whose hand is my soul, ten angels hastened with it, wanting to write it, but did not know how to write it until they raised it to the Possessor of Might, who said: Write it as My servant said."
"6458","And with the same chain; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A people will pass out of the religion as an arrow passes out of the target."
"6459","And with the same chain; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to enjoin marriage and strongly forbid celibacy, saying: Marry the loving and fertile, for I will outnumber the nations through you on the Day of Resurrection."
"6460","Ibrahim ibn Mujashshir narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Hafs, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to break the fast on the day of Fitr with dates, then go out."
"6461","Taliq ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Hafs, who said: When Anas ibn Malik wanted to combine two prayers while traveling, he delayed Zuhr to the end of its time, then prayed it, and prayed Asr at the beginning of its time; and he prayed Maghrib at the end of its time and prayed Isha at the beginning of its time, saying: Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to combine two prayers while traveling. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who corroborated Hafs ibn Ubaydullah in this narration; al-Zuhri narrated it differently from what Hafs narrated."
"6462","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abd al-Karim al-Azdi narrated to us; Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us; Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Many a disheveled, dusty one, disregarded, who if he swore by Allah, Allah would fulfill it. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Hafs except Usamah ibn Zayd, though it was narrated by other routes from Anas."
"6463","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa narrated to us; Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Hafs, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and after Fajr until the sun rises. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Hafs except Usamah ibn Zayd."
"6464","Uthman ibn Hafs narrated to us, from Amr al-Duri; Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us; Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Hafs, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere, except the Sacred Mosque. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Hafs except Ubaydullah, nor did anyone narrate it from Ubaydullah except Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi."
"6465","Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith narrated to us; Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us; Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Zayd al-Abdi, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Three registers will be brought forth for the son of Adam on the Day of Resurrection: a register containing righteous deeds, a register containing his sins, and a register containing the blessings of Allah upon him. Allah will say to the smallest blessing - I think he said: in the register of blessings: Take your price from his righteous deeds. His righteous deeds will be exhausted, then it will be set aside saying: By Your might, I have not been fully recompensed. The sins and blessings remain while all righteous deeds are gone. When Allah wills to have mercy on a servant, He says: O My servant, I have multiplied your good deeds for you, overlooked your evil deeds - I think he said: and bestowed My blessing upon you."
"6466","Al-Sakan ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Duba'i narrated to us; Maymun ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Siyah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No two Muslims meet and one takes the hand of his companion but that it is incumbent upon Allah not to part their hands until He forgives them."
"6467","Abu Kamil and Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us; Hazm ibn Abi Hazm narrated to us; Maymun ibn Siyah narrated to us, from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever loves delay in his term and increase in his provision, let him join his kin."
"6468","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Naji narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman narrated to us; Mansur ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Siyah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever prays Fajr is under the protection of Allah. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Maymun ibn Siyah except Mansur ibn Sa'd."
"6469","Al-Sakan ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Duba'i narrated to us; Maymun ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Siyah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No Muslim servant visits a brother of his for the sake of Allah but that a caller from heaven calls: You are blessed, and Paradise is blessed for you. Otherwise Allah says in the kingdom of His throne: My servant visited for My sake, and his hospitality is upon Me; and Allah is not pleased with any reward for him less than Paradise."
"6470","And with the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No people gather remembering Allah, seeking thereby only His face, but that a caller from heaven calls: Rise forgiven; your evil deeds have been replaced with good deeds."
"6471","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us; Khalaf ibn Uqbah informed us; Abu al-Zahra' narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says after the prayer: Glory be to Allah the Magnificent and with His praise; there is no power nor strength except through Allah, rises forgiven."
"6472","And with the same chain; he said: We entered upon Anas ibn Malik and he recited the Opening of the Book and: Say: He is Allah, the One, and said: It is a third of the Quran, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - meaning: Say: He is Allah, the One. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu al-Zahra' except Khalaf ibn Uqbah, nor do we know that he narrated from Anas except these two hadiths."
"6473","Amr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abd al-Karim narrated to us - the wording is Muhammad's - they said: Sa'id ibn Amir narrated to us; Shubayl ibn Azrah narrated to us, saying: I went to Anas ibn Malik and he narrated to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The example of the righteous companion is like the perfume-seller: if he does not give you of his perfume, some of its scent reaches you."
"6474","Abu Kurayb, Ibrahim ibn Sa'id, and al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us; they said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"6475","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Walid narrated to us; al-Haytham ibn Jamil narrated to us; Sallam ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A son of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam died and he grieved over him, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: O Messenger of Allah, whoever has three children die before reaching puberty, they will be his ransom from the Fire. And this hadith - none narrated it from Asim, from Anas, except Sallam, nor from Sallam except al-Haytham ibn Jamil."
"6476","Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari narrated to us; Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us; Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me the kunyah of a vegetable I used to gather - meaning Abu Hamzah. And this hadith - we heard it only from Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim from Aswad ibn Amir; rather it is preserved from Khaythamah Abu Nadr from Anas."
"6477","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us; Abu Ahmad narrated to us; Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O possessor of two ears. And this hadith - none narrated it except Sharik."
"6478","Muhammad ibn Abi al-Walid al-Fahham narrated to us; al-Waddah ibn Yahya narrated to us; Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to apply kohl an odd number of times. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu al-Ahwas from Asim."
"6479","Abu Bakr al-Adani narrated to us; Asid ibn Zayd narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to a Jew seeking a loan until ease, who said: And does he have ease, having neither crops nor udders?! That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The enemy of Allah has lied; I am the most faithful of them in repaying. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Asim, from Anas, except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash."
"6480","Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about al-Safa and al-Marwah, and he said: They were among the rites of ignorance, so when Islam came we refrained from them, then Allah revealed: Indeed al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah, so whoever performs Hajj to the House or Umrah, there is no blame upon him to circumambulate them."
"6481","And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us; al-Firyabi Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim, who said: I asked Anas about al-Safa and al-Marwah ... and he mentioned the like of it."
"6482","Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Abdullah ibn al-Ajlah narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Asim, from Anas, except Abdullah ibn al-Ajlah."
"6483","Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about qunut, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut before bowing. And this hadith - we do not know it narrated from Anas by a sound route except from Asim from Anas. The precise narrators among the companions of Anas narrated this hadith from Anas - among them Muhammad ibn Sirin, Abu Mijlaz, Qatadah, and others, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut after bowing."
"6484","Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-Aqadi narrated to us; Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated to us; Asim narrated to us, from Anas, who said: Wine was forbidden on the day it was forbidden while their drink that day was only unripe and ripe dates. And this hadith - we retain it from Asim only through the hadith of Fudayl ibn Sulayman."
"6485","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Wasiti narrated to us; Asim ibn Ali narrated to us; Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the sons of the Ansar, and the sons of the sons of the Ansar. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Asim except Qays ibn al-Rabi'."
"6486","Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Riqashi narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of the solitary, or the prayer of a man alone, by twenty-five prayers. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Asim, from Anas, except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"6487","Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us. And Sahl ibn Bahr narrated it to us; al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us; they said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not guide you to that by which Allah expiates sins? Perfecting ablution and many steps to the mosques. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Isam except Abu Bakr."
"6488","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas, who said: A people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge allegiance to him, among them a man with a trace of khaluq on his hand. He kept pledging them while delaying him, then said: The perfume of men is that whose scent is apparent and color hidden, and the perfume of women is that whose color is apparent and scent hidden. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Asim except Isma'il ibn Zakariyya."
"6489","Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Abdullah ibn al-Ajlah narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas, who said: Praying between graves was forbidden."
"6490","Yusuf al-Qattan narrated to us; Jarir narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between the Emigrants and the Ansar in our house."
"6491","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar narrated to us, from Thabit and Asim, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like pumpkin."
"6492","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Junayd narrated to us; Amr ibn Asim narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit and Asim, from Anas, who said: The Jews used to isolate women in menstruation, neither eating nor drinking with them, and expelling them from houses ... and he mentioned the hadith, which is in the hadith of Thabit, from Anas, in full."
"6493","Ahmad ibn Malik al-Qushayri narrated to us; Za'idah ibn Abi al-Ruqad narrated to us, from Ziyad al-Numayri, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Three expiations, three degrees, three salvations, and three destructions. As for the expiations: perfecting ablution in cold, awaiting prayers after prayers, and carrying feet to the Friday prayers. As for the degrees: feeding food, spreading peace, and praying at night while people sleep. As for the salvations: justice in anger and pleasure, moderation in poverty and wealth, and fear of Allah in secret and open. As for the destructions: obeyed stinginess, followed desire, and a man's admiration of himself."
"6494","And with the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The five prayers and Friday to Friday are expiations for what is between them, so long as major sins are avoided. And among Friday is an hour which no Muslim man or woman coincides with asking Allah therein for good but He gives him. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the five prayers is like an abundant river at the door of one of you, in which he bathes five times each day; what then remains of his dirt?"
"6495","And with the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Injustice is three: an injustice Allah does not forgive, an injustice He forgives, and an injustice Allah does not leave. As for the injustice Allah does not forgive, it is association, and Allah said: Indeed association is a great injustice. As for the injustice Allah forgives, it is the servants' wronging themselves between them and their Lord. As for the injustice Allah does not leave, it is servants wronging one another until He settles it among them."
"6496","And with the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah has traveling angels seeking circles of remembrance; when they come upon them they surround them, then send their scout to heaven to the Lord of Might, blessed and exalted. They say: Our Lord, we came upon servants of Yours magnifying Your blessings, reciting Your Book, sending blessings upon Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and asking You for their Hereafter and world. He, blessed and exalted, says: Cover them with My mercy. They say: O Lord, among them is so-and-so the erring one, who only embraced them in embrace. He, blessed and exalted, says: Cover them with My mercy; they are the companions with whom their companion suffers no misery."
"6497","And with the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The womb has a hook clinging to the Throne, speaking with an eloquent tongue: O Allah, join whoever joins me and sever whoever severs me. Allah, blessed and exalted, says: I am Allah, the Most Merciful, the Merciful; I derived the womb from My name, so whoever joins it I join him, and whoever cuts it I cut him."
"6498","And with the same chain; that when Rajab entered, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: O Allah, bless us in Rajab and Sha'ban and let us reach Ramadan. And when it was Friday night he would say: This is a radiant night and a luminous day."
"6499","And with the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he mentioned this fire of yours and said: It is a part of seventy parts of the fire of Hell, and it did not reach you until - I think he said: it was sprinkled twice with water to give you light. The fire of Hell is black and dark."
"6500","And with the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he raised the hadith to his Lord, blessed and exalted, saying: O son of Adam, if you draw near Me a handspan I draw near you a cubit; if you draw near Me a cubit I draw near you a fathom; if you come to Me in repentance I hasten. O son of Adam, were you to err until your sins reached the clouds of heaven then sought My forgiveness, I would forgive you, and I do not care."
"6501","And with the same chain; that Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was gloomy, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Abu Bakr, why do I see you gloomy? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I was with my cousin so-and-so last night while he was struggling with himself. He said: Did you not prompt him: There is no god but Allah? He said: I did prompt him. He said: Did he say it? He said: Yes. He said: Paradise has become due for him. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, how is it for the living? He said: It is more demolishing, more demolishing, more demolishing - three times - of their sins."
"6502","And with the same chain, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When you pass by the gardens of Paradise, graze. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the gardens of Paradise in the world? He said: Circles of remembrance. And Za'idah ibn Abi al-Ruqad is a man of Basra, Bahili; he narrated from Thabit, from Ziyad al-Numayri, and others. What he alone narrates is only written. Ziyad al-Numayri is unobjectionable; a group of Basrans narrated from him. Had we known these hadiths from other than Za'idah, we would have narrated them from him."
"6503","Muhammad ibn Shahid al-Samman and Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us; Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Abu Qudamah, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Hajj and Umrah in the talbiyah. The wording is Muhammad ibn Shahid's. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shu'bah except Rawh ibn Ubadah."
"6504","Khalid ibn Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Zurarah ibn Abi al-Halal narrated to us, that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it."
"6505","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us; Zurarah narrated to us, from Anas."
"6506","And Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib narrated it to us; al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us; my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey of his, and a driver called Anjashah was driving them, when the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: O Anjashah, gently with your driving of the glass vessels, or as he said. The wording is al-Taymi's wording from Anas."
"6507","Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Zurarah narrated to us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Zuhr when the sun declined, Asr while the sun was white and clear, Maghrib when the sun set, Isha when the twilight disappeared, and Fajr - sometimes he prayed it when dawn broke, sometimes he delayed it. Zurarah ibn Abi al-Halal is a well-known man of Basra; Shu'bah and others narrated from him."
"6508","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard my father say: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will learn for me what happened to Abu Jahl? Ibn Mas'ud said: I will. He went and found him struck by the two sons of Afra' until he had grown cold. He said: I took his beard and said: Are you Abu Jahl? He said: And he said: Is he but a man you killed, or his people killed?"
"6509","And with the same chain; he said: A man used to assign date-palms to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before Qurayzah was conquered for him. When it was conquered for him, he began returning to them what they had given him. My family had given him something and ordered me to come to him and ask him to return it to them, or part of it. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given it to Umm Ayman, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he gave them to me. Umm Ayman came, put the garment around my neck, and said: No, by Allah, I will not give them to you, since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave them to me. He said: O Umm Ayman, leave him and for you is such-and-such - I thought he said: he gave her more than them, or as he said. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Anas except al-Taymi, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from al-Taymi except al-Mu'tamir; the first also none narrated except al-Taymi."
"6510","And with the same chain; he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Every prophet asked a request, and every prophet has a supplication; so I have stored my supplication as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection."
"6511","And with the same chain; he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw Paradise and the Fire depicted for me in this wall; I never saw like today in good and evil."
"6512","Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us; al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard my father narrating from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pronouncing talbiyah for both together. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Taymi except al-Mu'tamir, and we heard it only from Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi."
"6513","Abu Kamil and Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated to us; Sahl ibn Ziyad narrated to us; Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Supplication between the call to prayer and the commencement is not rejected. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Taymi except Sahl ibn Ziyad and Amr ibn al-Nu'man."
"6514","Matar ibn Muhammad al-Sukkari narrated to us; Abd al-Mu'min ibn Salim narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: To pray Fajr and sit until the sun rises is more beloved to me - I think he said: than to free such-and-such of the children of Isma'il - I think he said in both: four slaves of the children of Isma'il. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Taymi except Abd al-Mu'min, and he was not corroborated in it."
"6515","Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Haddad al-Kufi narrated to us; Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a wedding feast for Safiyyah with hays. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sulayman al-Taymi except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Abu Bakr except Yahya ibn Adam, and we heard it only from Ja'far ibn Muhammad."
"6516","Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No abandonment beyond three days. And this hadith - al-Mu'tamir and others narrated it from Sulayman, from Anas, as stopped."
"6517","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, saying: I heard my father say: I heard Anas say: I was standing over the tribe serving them drink - I being the youngest of them - of their fadikh. He said: A man came and said: Wine has been forbidden. They said: Pour it out, O Anas. I said to Anas: What was their drink? He said: Ripe and unripe dates. Abu Bakr ibn Anas said: Anas was a witness, and that was their wine that day; and Anas did not deny that."
"6518","And with the same chain, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: No one remains who prayed both qiblahs except me."
"6519","And with the same chain; he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) confided a secret to me, and I never told anyone of it; Umm Sulaym asked me and I did not tell her."
"6520","Ali ibn Shu'ayb and Abdullah ibn Ayyub al-Makhrami narrated to us; Ali ibn Asim narrated to us; Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Anas, who said: A boy of ours of the Ansar said on the day of Hunayn: We shall not be defeated today for lack of numbers. No sooner had we met our enemy than the people fled. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon a mule of his, with Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith holding its bridle and al-Abbas his uncle holding its stirrup, and we were in a soft valley. The dust rose - none of us could see his palm - when a figure approached. He said to him: To you; who are you? He said: I am Abu Bakr, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, with some ten wounds upon him. Then another figure approached and he said: To you; who are you? He said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, with some ten wounds upon him. Then another figure approached with some twenty wounds and he said: To you; who are you? He said: Uthman ibn Affan, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. Then another figure approached with some ten wounds and he said: To you; who are you? He said: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. Then the people came forward, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is there no loud-voiced man to go and call among the people? A man went and shouted; no sooner did his voice fall upon their hearing than they came back returning. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) charged and the Muslims charged with him, so the polytheists were defeated. Durayd ibn al-Simmah withdrew upon a hill - or he said: upon a mound - with about six hundred. One of the people said to him: By Allah, I see a squadron approaching. He said: Leave them to me. He said: Their mark is such, of their appearance such. He said: No harm upon you; Quda'ah is going off in pursuit of the people. They said: By Allah, we see a rugged squadron approaching. He said: Leave them to me. He said: Their mark is such, of their appearance such. He said: No harm upon you; this is Sulaym. Then they said: We see a horseman approaching. He said: Woe to you! Alone? They said: Alone. He said: Leave him to me. They said: Turbaned with a black turban. Durayd said: That, by Allah, is al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, and he, by Allah, will kill you and expel you from this place of yours. He said: He turned to them and said: Why are these left here? He went with those who followed him, killed about three hundred, and cut off the head of Durayd ibn al-Simmah and placed it before him. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it with this wording except Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Sulayman except Ali ibn Asim."
"6521","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us; Khalid ibn Yazid, the pearl merchant, narrated to us; Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Anas, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Gentle and loves gentleness, and gives for gentleness what He does not give for harshness."
"6522","And with the same chain; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes out seeking knowledge is in the way of Allah until he returns. And this hadith - we do not know it narrated with this wording from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by this route."
"6523","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us; Khalid ibn Yazid informed us; Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi', from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you travel in fertile land, give the mounts their due, or their share; when you travel in barren land, hasten upon them. Upon you is night travel, for the earth is folded at night. When you halt, do not halt upon the roadway, for it is the shelter of every beast. And this hadith - we do not know it narrated in this completeness from Anas except by this route; al-Zuhri narrated some of its words from Anas."
"6524","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us; Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi', from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut until he died, and Abu Bakr until he died, and Umar until he died. And this hadith - we do not know it narrated from Anas except by this route, and from the hadith of Amr ibn Ubayd and Isma'il ibn Muslim from al-Hasan from Anas."
"6525","Amr ibn Isa al-Duba'i narrated to us; al-Fadl ibn al-Ala' narrated to us; Layth narrated to us, from Ubaydullah - meaning Ibn Zahr - from al-Rabi', from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first of people to come forth when they are raised, their leader when they arrive in delegation, their spokesman when they listen, and their bearer of glad tidings when they despair. The banner of generosity that day is in my hand; I am the noblest of the children of Adam before Allah, and no boast. A thousand servants circulate around me as though they are hidden pearls. And this hadith was narrated from Anas by other routes with different wordings; we mentioned each hadith of them in its place with its wording."
"6526","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us; Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Anas narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves the world upon sincerity to Allah, blessed and exalted, and His worship, associating nothing with Him, and establishing the prayer and giving the zakat, leaves it while Allah is pleased with him. And it is the religion of Allah which the messengers brought, and they conveyed it from their Lord before the plain statement of the hadiths and the differing of the desires. And the confirmation of that in the Book of Allah: (If they repent) — meaning: if they abandon the idols and their worship: (and establish the prayer and give the zakat, then leave their way free). And He said in another verse: (But if they repent and establish the prayer and give the zakat, then they are your brothers in religion). Abu Bakr said: The end of the hadith, in my view — and Allah knows best — is: ""leaves it while He is pleased with him""; and the rest, in my view, is from the speech of al-Rabi' ibn Anas."
"6527","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us; Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Anas narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade plundering, and said: Whoever plunders is not of us."
"6528","Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri narrated to us; Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us; Abu Ja'far al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi', from Anas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the guise of a traveling man and said: O Muhammad, what is Islam... Then he mentioned similar to the hadith of Umar and Ibn Umar. And al-Rabi' ibn Anas is righteous, there is no harm in him; his origin is from the people of al-Rayy, and he is not of the children of Anas ibn Malik."
"6529","Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Yazid al-Huna'i, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who divorced his wife three times, then a man married her and divorced her before touching her — is she lawful for the first one? He said: No, until the other tastes her little honey and she tastes his little honey. And this hadith — Shu'bah narrated it from Yahya ibn Yazid, from Anas, as a stopped narration."
"6530","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us; Marwan narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise and the Fire were displayed to me beyond this wall, and I have never seen the like of the good and the evil."
"6531","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us; Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us; Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Marwan, freedman of Hind bint al-Muhallab, that she sent him on an errand to Anas ibn Malik, and he heard him narrating to his companions that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting in fasting. And we do not know that Marwan, freedman of Hind, transmitted from Anas except these two hadiths."
"6532","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us; Abu Asim narrated to us; Uthman ibn Sa'd narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: When we supplicated we would say: O Allah, place upon us the prayer of a righteous people, who are neither sinful nor wicked, who stand the night and fast the day."
"6533","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us; Abu Asim narrated to us; Uthman ibn Sa'd narrated to us; Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned toward Bayt al-Maqdis while he was praying Zuhr, and he turned his face toward the Ka'bah, so the foolish among the people said: (What has turned them away from the qiblah they used to face)?"
"6534","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us; Abu Asim narrated to us; Uthman narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he traveled and alighted at a stopping place, would bid farewell to the stopping place with two rak'ahs, or with a prayer. And the hadiths of Uthman ibn Sa'd — we mentioned them only because their wordings differ from the wordings narrated from Anas."
"6535","Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar informed us, from Ash'ath ibn Abdillah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A man passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while there were people with him, and a man with him said: I love this one. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stand and inform him. So he stood up to him and informed him, and he said: May the One for whose sake you loved me love you. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ash'ath except Ma'mar."
"6536","Ahmad ibn Malik al-Qushayri narrated to us; Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Duba'i narrated to us; al-Nadr ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Sa'd al-Iskaf, from Muhammad ibn Ali, who said: Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Allah, blessed and exalted, loves three of your companions. Then he came to him and said: O Muhammad, Paradise longs for three of your companions. Anas ibn Malik said: So I wanted to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but I was in awe of him. Then I met Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: O Abu Bakr, I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Jibril, peace be upon him, said: O Muhammad, Paradise longs for three — perhaps you are of them. Then I met Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and said to him the like of that. Then I met Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and said to him the like of what I said to Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I shall ask him; if I am of them, I shall praise Allah, blessed and exalted, and if I am not of them, praise be to Allah, mighty and majestic. So he entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Anas informed me that Jibril, peace be upon him, came to you and said: Paradise longs for three of your companions; if I am of them — meaning: I shall praise Allah, blessed and exalted — and if I am not of them, I shall praise Allah, mighty and majestic. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are of them, and Ammar ibn Yasir — and he will witness with you scenes whose virtue is clear and whose reward is great — and Salman is of us, the People of the House, so take him as a companion. And this hadith — we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Anas with this chain, and we do not know anyone who narrated it except Ja'far ibn Sulayman from al-Nadr; and al-Nadr ibn Humayd and Sa'd al-Iskaf were not strong in hadith, though the people of knowledge narrated from them and tolerated their hadith."
"6537","Yahya ibn Hatim al-Askari narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Kufi narrated to us; Bassam al-Sayrafi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about the wage of the cupper, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped; Abu Taybah cupped him, and he gave him his wage."
"6538","Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us; Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, would open the recitation with (Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds) and would give a single salutation."
"6539","al-Hasan ibn Yunus al-Baghdadi narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us; Huraym — meaning Ibn Sufyan — narrated to us, from Layth — meaning Ibn Abi Sulaym — from Ayyub, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: We were forbidden to pray in an elevated mosque. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub except Layth, nor from Layth except Huraym. And the hadith of Jarir ibn Hazim from Ayyub, from Anas — that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah have mercy on them both, used to give a single salutation — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub except Jarir."
"6540","Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Kathir ibn Ufayr narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not give a wedding feast for any of his wives except for Safiyyah."
"6541","Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us; Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Humayd al-Tawil, who said: Seventy men of the Ansar were killed on the day of Bi'r Ma'unah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would supplicate against those who killed them for fifteen days in the prayer, after the bowing."
"6542","And with his chain; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped; Abu Taybah cupped him, and he gave him his wage, and he spoke to his masters and they lightened his levy. And these hadiths from Humayd are well known; we mentioned them only from Yahya ibn Sa'id because of the eminence of Yahya ibn Sa'id, and that he narrated from Anas and heard these hadiths from Humayd, and we wanted to make clear the eminence of Humayd, since Yahya ibn Sa'id would narrate from him."
"6543","Muhammad ibn al-Haytham Abu Abdillah al-Baghdadi narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Kathir ibn Ufayr narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Humayd, from Anas, that he heard him saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between Quraysh and the Ansar, so he established brotherhood between Sa'd ibn al-Rabi' and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf. Sa'd said to me: I have wealth, and it is between me and you in two halves, and I have two wives — so look, whichever of them is more beloved to you, I shall divorce her, and when she becomes lawful, marry her. He said: May Allah bless for you your family and your wealth; show me the market. So he showed him, and he did not return until he returned with dates and dried yogurt. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a trace of yellow and said: Mahyam? He said: I have married a woman of the Ansar. He said: What did you give her as dower? He said: The weight of a date-stone of gold. He said: Give a wedding feast, even if with a sheep. And this hadith — we mentioned it only because it is from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Humayd."
"6544","Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us; al-Sakan ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man being supported between two men, and he asked about him. They said: He vowed to perform Hajj on foot. He said: Command him to ride. al-Sakan ibn Isma'il said: Yunus ibn Ubayd had narrated it to me from Humayd, from Anas; then I met Humayd and he narrated it to me. And this hadith — others besides al-Sakan narrated it from Humayd, from Thabit, from Anas; but we wanted to mention it among the hadith of Yunus ibn Ubayd from Humayd. And we do not know that Yunus narrated from Humayd any hadith other than this one, except a hadith in which al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Marwazi erred, which he narrated from Ibn Zuray'."
"6545","al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Bazzar narrated to us; al-Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj; Ziyad ibn Sa'd informed us; Humayd al-Tawil informed us, who said: We were discussing the earnings of the cupper in the presence of Anas ibn Malik, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped; Abu Taybah cupped him, and he ordered a sa' of food for him, and he ordered his family to lighten his levy."
"6546","And with his chain, he said: I heard Anas saying: The best of what you treat yourselves with is cupping; and I think he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And we do not know that Ziyad ibn Sa'd transmitted from Humayd, from Anas, except these two hadiths; and we do not know anyone who narrated them from him except Ibn Jurayj, nor from Ibn Jurayj except al-Hajjaj."
"6547","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us; Ziyad ibn Abdillah narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: Usama ibn Zayd was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was a boy, and he saw Suhayl ibn Amr and said: O my father, is this not the one who used to feed us tharid in Makkah? And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept turning away from him. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Humayd, from Anas, with this wording except Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"6548","Muhammad ibn Sufyan al-Ubulli narrated to us; Badal ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Humayd — meaning al-Tawil — from Anas, who said: Allah did not disfigure him with any white hair — meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6549","And with his chain; that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in one of the streets of Madinah and heard a man saying: O Abu al-Qasim. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to him, and he said: I did not mean you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunyah."
"6550","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came to Madinah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between him and Sa'd ibn al-Rabi'. Sa'd offered to him, and Abd al-Rahman said to him: May Allah bless for you; show me the market. So he showed him the market, and he bought and sold. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a trace of yellow and said: Mahyam — or a word like it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have married a woman for the weight of a date-stone of gold. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give a wedding feast, even if with a sheep."
"6551","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us; Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came to Madinah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between him and Sa'd ibn al-Rabi'. Sa'd offered to him — I reckon he said: his wealth? — and he said: May Allah bless for you your family and your wealth; show me the market. So he entered the market and profited from dried yogurt and clarified butter. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him after some days with a trace of yellow upon him and said: Mahyam, O Abd al-Rahman? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have married a woman of the Ansar. He said: What did you give her as dower? He said: The weight of a date-stone of gold. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give a wedding feast, even if with a sheep."
"6552","al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us; Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave him his wage."
"6553","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: Abu Taybah cupped the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave him a sa', or two sa's, of food, and he spoke to his masters and they lightened his burden."
"6554","Muhammad ibn Mirdas al-Ansari narrated to us; Mujja'ah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dug the Trench, the Ansar said that day: al-jihad. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, indeed the good is the good of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirah."
"6555","Abu Kamil narrated to us; Abu Ahmad narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the prayer and spat into his garment, gathering part of it to part."
"6556","Zuhayr ibn Muhammad ibn Qumayr narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas — Abd al-Razzaq said: and Sufyan informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, and the wording is the wording of Thabit — that he wanted to marry a woman, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Look at her, for it is more likely to bring lasting affection between you. So al-Mughira ibn Shu'bah married her. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Thawri except Abd al-Razzaq."
"6557","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mufaddal al-Harrani narrated to us; Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Harrani narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The text ends here in the source without the wording of the hadith.]"
"6558","And Ahmad ibn Bakkar al-Bahili narrated to us; al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over al-Najashi when the news of his death came, and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, do you pray over an Abyssinian slave?! So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: (And indeed among the People of the Book are those who believe in Allah)."
"6559","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mufaddal al-Harrani narrated to us; Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Close for me every door into the mosque except the door of Abu Bakr; and had I taken a close friend I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Humayd except Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit, nor from Abd al-Rahman except Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman; and many people narrated it from Uthman and tolerated his hadith."
"6560","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us; al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who is the most beloved of people to you? He said: A'ishah. He said: Among men? He said: Then her father. And this is a hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it from Humayd, from Anas, except al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman, and we heard it only from Ahmad ibn Abdah."
"6561","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna ibn Ubayd ibn Musa narrated to us; Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik — if Allah wills — who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by an outstretched rope and said: What is this rope? They said: So-and-so prays; when she is overcome she holds onto it. He said: Let her pray as long as she understands; when she is overcome, let her sleep. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Anas except Humayd."
"6562","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas — if Allah wills — who said: The Muslims heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calling at night over the well of Badr: O Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, and O Utbah ibn Rabi'ah, and O Shaybah ibn Rabi'ah, and O Umayyah ibn Khalaf — have you found what your Lord promised you to be true? For I have found what my Lord promised me to be true. They said: O Messenger of Allah, do you call out to a people who have become carcasses? He said: You are not more hearing of what I say than they are, except that they are unable to answer. And this hadith — we do not know anyone who narrated it with this wording from Anas except Humayd; and Thabit narrated some of this speech."
"6563","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marched to Badr and consulted the Muslims; Abu Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him, advised him, then he consulted Umar and he advised him, may Allah have mercy on him, then he consulted them, and the Ansar said: O company of the Ansar, it is you whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) means. They said: Then we shall not say what the Children of Isra'il said to Musa, peace be upon him: Go, you and your Lord, and fight. By the One Who sent you with the truth, if you were to strike with us at its innards as far as Bark al-Ghimad, we would follow you."
"6564","And with his chain, he said: When the Muslims were routed on the day of Hunayn, and Umm Sulaym was with them, she kept calling out: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they have been routed — or a word like it. He said: O Umm Sulaym, Allah, blessed and exalted, has sufficed. He said: And Abu Talhah found a pickaxe and said: What is this, O Umm Sulaym? She said: I have held onto it; if any of the polytheists comes near me, I shall rip open his belly. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, hear what Umm Sulaym is saying."
"6565","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: Submit. He said: I find myself averse. He said: Submit, even if you are averse."
"6566","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas stood in the place of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: We shall protect you from what we protect ourselves and our children from — so what is ours? He said: Paradise. He said: We are content."
"6567","And with his chain — if Allah wills — he said: We reached Sidrat al-Muntaha, and its lote-fruits were like jars, and its leaves like the ears of elephants; and when there covered it of the command of Allah what covered it, it transformed as Allah willed."
"6568","And with his chain — if Allah wills — he said: Abdullah ibn Salam came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon his arrival in Madinah and said: I shall ask you about three things which none knows but a prophet: the first food the people of Paradise eat, the child resembling his father or his mother, and the first of the signs of the Hour? He said: Jibril informed me of them just now. Abdullah ibn Salam said: The enemy of the Jews among the angels. He said: The first of the signs of the Hour: a fire that gathers them from the east to the west. As for the first food the people of Paradise eat: the extra lobe of the liver of a whale. As for the child: when the water of the man precedes, it draws it to itself; and when the water of the woman precedes, she draws it to herself. He said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews are a slanderous people; if they learn of my Islam before you ask them about me, they will slander me in your presence. So he sent for the Jews and said: What kind of man is Abdullah ibn Salam? They said: Our best and the son of our best, our chief and the son of our chief, and our most learned. He said: What would you think if Abdullah ibn Salam were to submit? They said: Allah forbid him from that. Then Abdullah ibn Salam came out to them and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. They said: Rather, he is our worst — and they disparaged him. So Abdullah ibn Salam said: This is what I feared, O Messenger of Allah."
"6569","And with his chain, he said: The front tooth of al-Rubayyi' was broken, so they requested of them to pardon, but they refused them anything but retaliation. So Anas ibn al-Nadr said: O Messenger of Allah, shall the molar tooth of al-Rubayyi' be broken? By the One Who sent you with the truth, it shall not be broken. So he said: O Anas, the Book of Allah is retaliation. He said: Then the people agreed and pardoned. So he said: Among the servants of Allah are those who, if they swear by Allah, blessed and exalted, He fulfills their oath."
"6570","And with his chain, he said: A man came and reached the people while out of breath, and when he stood in the prayer he said: Praise be to Allah, much good blessed praise. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: Who is the speaker — or: who is the sayer? The people fell silent. Then he said: Who is the speaker — or: who is the sayer? For he has done well — or he said: he has said no wrong. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I reached the row out of breath — or he said: my breath urged me on. He said: I saw twelve angels racing to it, which of them would raise it. Then he said: When one of you comes to the prayer, let him walk in his manner; let him pray what he catches and make up what he missed."
"6571","And with his chain, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swore an oath of abstention from his wives for a month. The people came to him, the prayer came, and he prayed with them sitting while they were standing. When the next prayer came, they went to stand, so he said: Follow your imam; when he prays sitting, pray sitting, and when he prays standing, pray standing. So he stayed twenty-nine nights, then he left off. They said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not swear an oath for a month? He said: The month is twenty-nine days. And the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""If he prays sitting, pray sitting"" is abrogated; his act, (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), at his death abrogated it, for he prayed sitting while the people stood behind him — and only the last of his acts is taken."
"6572","And with his chain — if Allah wills — he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the time of the morning prayer, so he prayed when dawn broke, then he delayed until it was light afterwards, then he said: Where is the questioner about the time of the morning prayer? What is between these two is the time."
"6573","And with his chain, he said: Banu Salimah wanted to move from their homes to near the mosque, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked that and said: O Banu Salimah, will you not count your footsteps as reward? So they stayed."
"6574","And with his chain, he said: The prayer was established, and he turned to us with his face before saying the takbir, and said: Stand close together, for I see you behind my back."
"6575","And with his chain; that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for the prayer, then turned to us with his face and said: Stand close together, stand close together, for I see you from behind my back."
"6576","And with his chain, he said: He would stand praying at night in one of his rooms, and some Muslims came to pray with his prayer. So he prayed, then he entered his house as Allah willed, then he came out to them; he did that repeatedly. When morning came they said: O Messenger of Allah, we prayed tonight with you, and we love to imitate your prayer. He said: I knew your place, and I did it deliberately."
"6577","And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a she-camel called al-Adba' which was not outrun. Then a Bedouin came upon a young camel and outran her, and it weighed heavily upon the Muslims. When he saw what was in their faces, they said: O Messenger of Allah, al-Adba' has been outrun. He said: It is a right upon Allah, mighty and majestic, that He does not raise anything of this world but that He lowers it."
"6578","And with his chain, he said: A man recited al-Baqarah and Al Imran, and he used to write in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He would dictate to him something of the names of Allah, blessed and exalted, and he would say: All-Hearing, All-Knowing, and the other would say: Forgiving, Merciful. He would say: Write whichever of them you wish. Then he apostatized from Islam and joined the polytheists, and said: Do you teach me about Muhammad? I used to write as I wished. Then he died, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earth will not accept him. He said: And it was mentioned that Abu Talhah came to the land in which the man died and found him cast out. He said: What is the matter with this one? They said: We buried him repeatedly, but the earth would not accept him. And this hadith — Thabit narrated it from Anas; and I think Humayd heard it from Thabit, and Thabit was not followed upon it."
"6579","And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best quarters of the Ansar? The quarters of Banu al-Najjar, then the quarters of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then the quarters of Banu al-Harith, then al-Khazraj, then the quarters of Banu Sa'idah; and in all the quarters of the Ansar there is good."
"6580","And with his chain — if Allah wills — he said: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was moderate, and the prayer of Abu Bakr; and Umar extended in the morning prayer."
"6581","And with his chain, he said: There was a boy on the road, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by with some people. When the boy's mother saw the people, she feared her son would be trampled, so she hastened and carried him, saying: My son, my son. The people said: O Messenger of Allah, this one would not cast her son into the Fire. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nor will Allah cast His beloved into the Fire."
"6582","And with his chain — if Allah wills — he said: A woman presented herself to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a need of you. He said: O mother of so-and-so, sit at whichever side of the streets you wish and I shall sit with you. So she sat and he sat with her until he fulfilled her need."
"6583","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A morning excursion in the path of Allah, or an evening excursion, is better than the world and what is in it; and the space of the bow of one of you is better than the world and what is in it. And were a woman of the people of Paradise to look down upon the people of the earth, she would fill what is between them with fragrance; and her head-cover upon her head is better than the world and what is in it. And this hadith — more than one narrated it from Humayd, from Anas, as stopped; and Thabit narrated some of its wording."
"6584","Ibn Muthanna narrated to us; Khalid narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, who said: Anas said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with one of the Mothers of the Believers, and she sent to him a bowl containing food. Then she struck the hand of the messenger and the bowl fell and broke. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took one of the two pieces and joined one to the other, gathering the food in them, saying: Your mother has become jealous. They ate until she came with a bowl from her own house. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed the sound bowl to the messenger and left the broken one in the house of the one who broke it."
"6585","And Muhammad ibn Salih al-Baghdadi narrated it to us; Harmalah narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abdillah ibn Salim narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"6586","And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until it ripens. We said: O Abu Hamzah, what is its ripening? He said: It reddens and yellows."
"6587","And with his chain — if Allah wills — he said: I entered Paradise and there I was with a palace of gold. I said: Whose palace is this? They said: For a young man of Quraysh. I thought I was he. They said: Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"6588","And Ibn Muthanna narrated it to us; Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and there I was with a palace of gold. I said: Whose palace is this? They said: For a young man of Quraysh. I said: For whom? They said: For Umar ibn al-Khattab. Had I not known of your jealousy, I would have entered it. Umar said: Over you, O Messenger of Allah, should I be jealous?"
"6589","And with his first chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us while I was a boy among boys, and he greeted us. Then he took my hand and sent me on an errand, and sat in the shade of a wall until I returned. When I came to Umm Sulaym, she said: What kept you? I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me on an errand. She said: And what is it? I said: It is a secret. She said: Guard the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And I never informed anyone of it at all."
"6590","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us; Ibn Abi Adiyy and Isma'il ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"6591","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib narrated to us; al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, with similar to the hadith of Khalid ibn al-Harith — except that in the hadith of al-Taymi there is not: ""and he greeted us."""
"6592","And with the first chain, he said: Anas said: The front tooth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was broken on the day of Uhud, and he was wounded, and blood began to flow upon his face; he would wipe the blood from his face and say: How shall a people prosper who have stained the face of their prophet with blood while he calls them to their Lord? So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: (Not for you is the decision, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for indeed they are wrongdoers). And this hadith — Thabit narrated it; and Humayd is more complete in wording for it than Thabit."
"6593","And with his chain, he said: When this verse was revealed: (You will never attain righteousness until you spend of what you love) — or: (Who is it that would loan Allah a goodly loan) — Abu Talhah said: O Messenger of Allah, my walled garden in such-and-such place is for Allah, blessed and exalted; and had I been able to conceal it, I would not have announced it. He said: Place it among the poor of your family, or among the people of your house."
"6594","And with his chain, he said: Anas was asked about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his voluntary fasting? He said: He would fast of the month until we would say: He does not intend to break fast at all; and he would break fast of the month until we would say: He does not intend to fast any of it. And whenever we wished to see him at night praying, we saw him; and we never saw him sleeping but that we saw him."
"6595","Abd al-Wahid narrated it to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, from Anas. [The preceding speech about fasting — Hammad narrated some of its wording from Thabit, from Anas, specifically concerning fasting.]"
"6596","And with his chain, he said: Anas said: Abu Musa al-Ash'ari came seeking mounts from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and found him occupied. So he said: By Allah, I shall not mount you. When he turned his back, he called him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you swore you would not mount me. He said: And I swear I shall mount you. So he mounted him. And the meaning of this hadith, in our view, is upon what was narrated from him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in other than this hadith, saying: I do not swear an oath and then see another better than it, except that I do what is better."
"6597","And with his chain, he said: Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall come to you peoples whose hearts are more tender than yours. Then the Ash'aris came."
"6598","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Khalid ibn al-Harith, Sahl ibn Yusuf and Ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas — Ibn Abi Adiyy and Sahl ibn Yusuf raised it, while Khalid did not raise it — who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you wish for death because of harm that has befallen him; rather let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and take me when death is good for me. And this hadith — others besides those we named narrated it from Humayd, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with other than this wording."
"6599","And with his first chain, he said: Anas said: Umm Sulaym took me upon the arrival of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah and said: O Messenger of Allah, Anas is a boy who writes; he shall serve you. So I served him nine years, and he never said to me concerning anything I did: You did wrong — nor: What an evil thing you did."
"6600","And with his chain, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and heard a movement before me, and there I was with al-Ghumaysa' bint Milhan. Humayd said: And she is Umm Sulaym."
